1
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,795
<i>Report to your stations immediately.</i>

2
00:00:44,962 --> 00:00:46,589
<i>This is not a drill.</i>

3
00:00:46,631 --> 00:00:47,715
<i>We are under attack!</i>

4
00:00:49,133 --> 00:00:51,093
<i>We are under attack!</i>

5
00:01:52,196 --> 00:01:54,490
- Shit!
- Language!

6
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:56,200
Jarvis, what's the view from upstairs?

7
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:57,660
<i>The central building is</i>

8
00:01:57,743 --> 00:02:00,288
<i>protected by some kind of energy shield.</i>

9
00:02:00,788 --> 00:02:02,248
<i>Strucker's technology is well beyond</i>

10
00:02:02,373 --> 00:02:04,500
<i>any other Hydra base we've taken.</i>

11
00:02:07,378 --> 00:02:08,921
Loki's scepter must be here.

12
00:02:09,547 --> 00:02:11,215
Strucker couldn't mount
this defense without it.

13
00:02:12,174 --> 00:02:13,718
At long last.

14
00:02:25,187 --> 00:02:27,398
"At long last" is lasting a little long, boys.

15
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,822
Yeah. I think we lost
the element of surprise.

16
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:38,617
Wait a second. No one else
is gonna deal with the fact

17
00:02:38,743 --> 00:02:40,536
that Cap just said "Language"?

18
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,204
I know.

19
00:02:47,251 --> 00:02:49,503
Just slipped out.

20
00:02:55,593 --> 00:02:57,345
Who gave the order to attack?

21
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:59,764
<i>Herr</i> Strucker, it's the Avengers.

22
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,767
They landed in the far woods.
The perimeter guard panicked.

23
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,852
They have to be after the scepter.

24
00:03:06,062 --> 00:03:08,439
- Can we hold them?
- They're the Avengers.

25
00:03:08,564 --> 00:03:10,149
Deploy the rest of the tanks.

26
00:03:10,316 --> 00:03:12,193
Concentrate fire on the weak ones.

27
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,695
A hit may make them close ranks.

28
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,115
Everything we've accomplished...

29
00:03:18,282 --> 00:03:20,618
But we're on the verge of our
greatest breakthrough.

30
00:03:20,785 --> 00:03:22,411
Then let's show them
what we've accomplished.

31
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:24,205
Send out the twins.

32
00:03:25,498 --> 00:03:27,291
It's too soon.

33
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:29,502
It's what they signed up for.

34
00:03:30,086 --> 00:03:32,004
My men can hold them.

35
00:03:39,637 --> 00:03:41,514
<i>Sir, the city is taking fire.</i>

36
00:03:44,392 --> 00:03:47,895
Well, we know Strucker's not gonna
worry about civilian casualties.

37
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,688
Send in the Iron Legion.

38
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:57,488
<i>This quadrant is unsafe.
Please back away.</i>

39
00:03:58,406 --> 00:03:59,990
<i>We are here to help.</i>

40
00:04:01,117 --> 00:04:03,494
<i>This quadrant is unsafe.
Please back away.</i>

41
00:04:05,246 --> 00:04:06,330
<i>Please back away.</i>

42
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:08,541
- <i>We wish to avoid collateral damage.</i>
- Costel!

43
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:11,168
<i>We will inform you when this
current conflict is resolved.</i>

44
00:04:11,293 --> 00:04:13,337
- <i>We are here to help.</i>
- Avengers, go home!

45
00:04:15,756 --> 00:04:16,924
<i>We are here to help.</i>

46
00:04:18,008 --> 00:04:19,844
<i>We will not yield!</i>

47
00:04:20,469 --> 00:04:23,764
The Americans sent their
circus freaks to test us.

48
00:04:24,348 --> 00:04:26,809
We will send them back in bags.

49
00:04:29,145 --> 00:04:32,022
- No surrender!
- No surrender!

50
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,067
I am going to surrender.

51
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:37,153
You delete everything.

52
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:39,071
If we give the Avengers the weapons,

53
00:04:39,196 --> 00:04:40,698
they may not look too far
into what we've been...

54
00:04:40,823 --> 00:04:42,908
- The twins.
- They are not ready to take on...

55
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:45,244
No, no, I mean...

56
00:04:45,369 --> 00:04:46,829
Twins.

57
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:15,065
You didn't see that coming?

58
00:05:21,363 --> 00:05:23,699
Clint!

59
00:05:25,743 --> 00:05:27,036
We have an Enhanced in the field.

60
00:05:27,161 --> 00:05:28,162
Clint's hit!

61
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:34,043
Somebody want to deal with that bunker?

62
00:05:38,088 --> 00:05:39,298
Thank you.

63
00:05:46,388 --> 00:05:48,891
Stark, we really need to get inside.

64
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:50,267
I'm closing in.

65
00:05:53,395 --> 00:05:55,523
Jarvis, am I closing in?

66
00:05:56,524 --> 00:05:58,442
Do you see a power
source for that shield?

67
00:05:58,609 --> 00:06:01,111
<i>There's a particle wave
below the north tower.</i>

68
00:06:01,237 --> 00:06:03,239
Great, I want to poke it with something.

69
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,123
The drawbridge is down, people.

70
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:19,296
- The Enhanced?
- He's a blur.

71
00:06:19,964 --> 00:06:21,966
All the new players we've faced,
I've never seen this.

72
00:06:22,466 --> 00:06:23,759
In fact, I still haven't.

73
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:26,178
<i>Clint's hit pretty bad, guys.
We're gonna need evac.</i>

74
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,763
I can get Barton to the jet.

75
00:06:27,888 --> 00:06:29,223
The sooner we're gone, the better.

76
00:06:29,390 --> 00:06:30,516
You and Stark secure the scepter.

77
00:06:30,641 --> 00:06:31,725
Copy that.

78
00:06:32,977 --> 00:06:34,770
Looks like they're lining up.

79
00:06:35,062 --> 00:06:36,564
Well, they're excited.

80
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:41,819
Find the scepter.

81
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,989
And for gosh sake, watch your language!

82
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:48,409
That's not going away any time soon.

83
00:06:54,331 --> 00:06:56,500
Guys, stop. We gotta talk this through.

84
00:06:59,503 --> 00:07:00,754
<i>It was a good talk.</i>

85
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:02,172
No, it wasn't.

86
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:05,593
Oh!

87
00:07:08,345 --> 00:07:10,264
Sentry mode.

88
00:07:12,641 --> 00:07:14,518
Okay, Jarvis, you know. I want it all.

89
00:07:14,685 --> 00:07:16,604
Make sure you copy Hill at HQ.

90
00:07:20,983 --> 00:07:22,276
We're locked down out here.

91
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,945
Then get to Banner. Time for a lullaby.

92
00:07:28,699 --> 00:07:30,743
I know you're hiding more than files.

93
00:07:31,952 --> 00:07:34,580
Hey, J, give me an IR scan
of the room, real quick.

94
00:07:34,705 --> 00:07:36,248
<i>The wall to your left.</i>

95
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:38,000
<i>I'm reading steel reinforcement</i>

96
00:07:39,251 --> 00:07:40,878
<i>and an air current.</i>

97
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:42,212
Please be a secret door.

98
00:07:42,379 --> 00:07:44,214
Please be a secret door.
Please be a secret door.

99
00:07:44,923 --> 00:07:45,924
Yay.

100
00:08:02,191 --> 00:08:04,109
Hey, big guy.

101
00:08:06,487 --> 00:08:08,113
Sun's getting real low.

102
00:09:12,219 --> 00:09:13,804
Baron Strucker.

103
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:16,223
Hydra's number one thug.

104
00:09:16,974 --> 00:09:19,476
Technically, I'm a thug for S.H.I.E.L.D.

105
00:09:19,643 --> 00:09:21,687
Well, then technically you're unemployed.

106
00:09:22,104 --> 00:09:23,772
Where's Loki's scepter?

107
00:09:23,897 --> 00:09:25,816
Don't worry, I know when I'm beat.

108
00:09:26,734 --> 00:09:29,278
You'll mention how I cooperated, I hope.

109
00:09:29,445 --> 00:09:31,864
I'll put it right under "illegal
human experimentation."

110
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:34,533
How many are there?

111
00:09:39,496 --> 00:09:42,416
We have a second Enhanced.
Female. Do not engage.

112
00:09:43,834 --> 00:09:45,335
You'll have to be faster than...

113
00:09:50,507 --> 00:09:52,176
<i>Guys, I got Strucker.</i>

114
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:55,763
Yeah, I got something bigger.

115
00:10:19,036 --> 00:10:20,287
<i>Thor,</i>

116
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:23,040
I got eyes on the prize.

117
00:11:12,881 --> 00:11:16,260
You could have saved us.

118
00:11:24,268 --> 00:11:26,228
<i>Why didn't you do more?</i>

119
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:05,559
We're just gonna let him take it?

120
00:12:57,444 --> 00:12:59,696
Hey, the lullaby worked better than ever.

121
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,367
Just wasn't expecting a code green.

122
00:13:03,450 --> 00:13:04,534
You hadn't been there,

123
00:13:04,576 --> 00:13:07,412
there would have been
double the casualties.

124
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:10,040
My best friend would've been
a treasured memory.

125
00:13:10,791 --> 00:13:12,709
You know, sometimes exactly
what I want to hear

126
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:14,628
isn't exactly what I want to hear.

127
00:13:15,796 --> 00:13:17,714
How long before you trust me?

128
00:13:19,716 --> 00:13:21,426
It's not you I don't trust.

129
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,055
Thor, report on the Hulk.

130
00:13:25,222 --> 00:13:28,100
The gates of Hel are filled
with the screams of his victims.

131
00:13:30,102 --> 00:13:33,105
But not the screams of the dead, of course.
No, no, wounded screams.

132
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:35,440
Mainly whimpering,
a great deal of complaining

133
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:39,569
and tales of sprained deltoids and gout.

134
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:42,906
Hey, Banner, Dr. Cho is
on her way in from Seoul.

135
00:13:43,073 --> 00:13:44,533
Is it okay if she sets up in your lab?

136
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:46,576
Uh, yeah, she knows her way around.

137
00:13:46,743 --> 00:13:47,953
Thanks. Tell her to prep everything.

138
00:13:48,078 --> 00:13:49,413
Barton's gonna need the full treatment.

139
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:51,415
- <i>Very good, sir.</i>
- Jarvis, take the wheel.

140
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:52,874
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

141
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,876
<i>Approach vector is locked.</i>

142
00:13:55,043 --> 00:13:57,421
Feels good, yeah?

143
00:13:57,546 --> 00:13:59,631
I mean, you've been after this thing
since S.H.I.E.L.D. collapsed.

144
00:13:59,756 --> 00:14:01,800
Not that I haven't enjoyed
our little raiding parties, but...

145
00:14:01,925 --> 00:14:04,302
No, but this... This brings it to a close.

146
00:14:05,095 --> 00:14:06,930
As soon as we find out what else
this has been used for.

147
00:14:07,097 --> 00:14:08,265
I don't just mean weapons.

148
00:14:08,807 --> 00:14:11,101
Since when is Strucker capable
of human enhancement?

149
00:14:11,268 --> 00:14:13,520
Banner and I will give it the once over
before it goes back to Asgard.

150
00:14:13,645 --> 00:14:14,688
Is that cool with you?

151
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:16,815
Just a few days till the farewell party.

152
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:19,067
You're staying, right?

153
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:21,903
Yes, yes, of course.
A victory should be honored with revels.

154
00:14:22,029 --> 00:14:24,781
Yeah, who doesn't love revels? Captain?

155
00:14:24,948 --> 00:14:27,826
Hopefully this puts an end
to the Chitauri and Hydra.

156
00:14:27,951 --> 00:14:29,578
So, yes, revels.

157
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:04,696
Lab's all set up, boss.

158
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:05,947
Oh, actually, he's the boss.

159
00:15:06,073 --> 00:15:08,492
I just pay for everything
and design everything

160
00:15:08,658 --> 00:15:10,160
and make everyone look cooler.

161
00:15:10,327 --> 00:15:11,661
What's the word on Strucker?

162
00:15:11,787 --> 00:15:13,830
- NATO's got him.
- The two Enhanced?

163
00:15:13,955 --> 00:15:16,541
Wanda and Pietro Maximoff. Twins.

164
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:19,503
Orphaned at 10 when a shell
collapsed their apartment building.

165
00:15:19,878 --> 00:15:22,172
Sokovia's had a rough history.

166
00:15:22,339 --> 00:15:25,717
It's nowhere special, but it's on the way
to everywhere special.

167
00:15:25,842 --> 00:15:27,010
Their abilities?

168
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:28,178
He's got increased metabolism

169
00:15:28,345 --> 00:15:29,971
and improved thermal homeostasis.

170
00:15:30,138 --> 00:15:32,182
Her thing is neuroelectric interfacing,

171
00:15:32,307 --> 00:15:34,392
telekinesis, mental manipulation.

172
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:36,645
He's fast and she's weird.

173
00:15:37,479 --> 00:15:39,564
Well, they're gonna show up again.

174
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:41,608
Agreed. File says they volunteered

175
00:15:41,733 --> 00:15:43,527
for Strucker's experiments.

176
00:15:43,652 --> 00:15:45,529
- It's nuts.
- Right.

177
00:15:45,695 --> 00:15:48,824
What kind of monster would let
a German scientist experiment on them

178
00:15:48,949 --> 00:15:50,200
to protect their country?

179
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:52,077
We're not at war, Captain.

180
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:53,912
They are.

181
00:16:24,025 --> 00:16:25,360
How's he doing?

182
00:16:25,485 --> 00:16:26,736
Unfortunately, he's still Barton.

183
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,196
That's terrible.

184
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:29,906
He's fine. He's thirsty.

185
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:32,909
All right. Look alive, Jarvis. It's playtime.

186
00:16:33,034 --> 00:16:35,036
We've only got a couple
of days with this joystick,

187
00:16:35,162 --> 00:16:37,080
so let's make the most of it.

188
00:16:37,247 --> 00:16:40,750
Update me on the structural
and compositional analysis.

189
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:43,920
<i>The scepter is alien.</i>

190
00:16:44,087 --> 00:16:46,089
<i>There are elements I can't quantify.</i>

191
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:47,591
So there's elements you can?

192
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:49,759
<i>The jewel appears to be
a protective housing</i>

193
00:16:49,885 --> 00:16:51,303
<i>for something inside,</i>

194
00:16:51,428 --> 00:16:52,762
<i>something powerful.</i>

195
00:16:52,888 --> 00:16:53,972
Like a reactor?

196
00:16:54,097 --> 00:16:55,307
<i>Like a computer.</i>

197
00:16:55,432 --> 00:16:57,601
<i>I believe I'm deciphering code.</i>

198
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:01,479
Are you sure he's gonna be okay?

199
00:17:02,814 --> 00:17:05,108
Pretending to need this guy really
brings the team together.

200
00:17:05,275 --> 00:17:07,777
There's no possibility of deterioration.

201
00:17:07,944 --> 00:17:11,031
The nano-molecular functionality
is instantaneous.

202
00:17:11,156 --> 00:17:13,116
His cells don't know they're
bonding with simulacra.

203
00:17:13,283 --> 00:17:15,160
She's creating tissue.

204
00:17:15,285 --> 00:17:16,661
If you brought him to my lab,

205
00:17:16,786 --> 00:17:19,414
the Regeneration Cradle
could do this in 20 minutes.

206
00:17:19,539 --> 00:17:21,458
Oh, he's flat-lining. Call it. Time?

207
00:17:21,625 --> 00:17:24,002
No, no, no, I'm gonna live forever.

208
00:17:24,127 --> 00:17:25,670
I'm gonna be made of plastic.

209
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,130
Here's your beverage.

210
00:17:27,255 --> 00:17:28,965
You'll be made of you, Mr. Barton.

211
00:17:29,132 --> 00:17:30,675
Your own girlfriend won't be
able to tell the difference.

212
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:31,927
I don't have a girlfriend.

213
00:17:32,052 --> 00:17:33,303
That I can't fix.

214
00:17:34,179 --> 00:17:36,139
This is the next thing, Tony.

215
00:17:36,306 --> 00:17:38,308
Your clunky metal suits are
gonna be left in the dust.

216
00:17:38,475 --> 00:17:40,185
That is exactly the plan.

217
00:17:41,144 --> 00:17:43,980
And, Helen, I expect to see you
at the party on Saturday.

218
00:17:44,147 --> 00:17:46,566
Unlike you, I don't have
a lot of time for parties.

219
00:17:48,026 --> 00:17:49,819
Will Thor be there?

220
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:54,324
- What's the rumpus?
- Well, the scepter.

221
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:59,120
You see, we were wondering
how Strucker got so inventive.

222
00:17:59,246 --> 00:18:03,166
So I've been analyzing the gem inside.

223
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:05,669
You may recognize...

224
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:08,505
- Jarvis.
<i>- Doctor.</i>

225
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:12,592
Started out, Jarvis was just
a natural language UI.

226
00:18:12,717 --> 00:18:13,760
Now he runs the Iron Legion.

227
00:18:14,302 --> 00:18:15,512
He runs more of the business

228
00:18:15,637 --> 00:18:18,014
- than anyone besides Pepper.
- Oh.

229
00:18:18,139 --> 00:18:19,224
- Top of the line.
- Yes.

230
00:18:19,349 --> 00:18:20,642
<i>I suspect not for long.</i>

231
00:18:21,851 --> 00:18:22,936
Meet the competition.

232
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,193
- It's beautiful.
- If you had to guess,

233
00:18:30,318 --> 00:18:33,321
- what's it look like it's doing?
- Like it's thinking.

234
00:18:34,072 --> 00:18:35,865
I mean, this could be...

235
00:18:36,324 --> 00:18:38,410
- It's not a human mind.
- Mmm-mmm.

236
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:40,537
I mean, look at this.

237
00:18:40,704 --> 00:18:42,872
They're like neurons firing.

238
00:18:43,498 --> 00:18:46,543
Down in Strucker's lab, I saw some
fairly advanced robotics work.

239
00:18:47,669 --> 00:18:50,255
They deep-sixed the data,

240
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:53,466
but I gotta guess he was
knocking on a very particular door.

241
00:18:55,427 --> 00:18:56,761
Artificial intelligence.

242
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:02,642
This could be it, Bruce.
This could be the key to creating Ultron.

243
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:06,604
I thought Ultron was a fantasy.

244
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:07,981
Yesterday it was.

245
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:11,151
If we can harness this power,

246
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:13,320
apply it to my Iron Legion protocol?

247
00:19:14,112 --> 00:19:16,072
That's a man-sized "if."

248
00:19:16,239 --> 00:19:18,575
Our job is "if."

249
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,286
What if you were sipping margaritas
on a sun-drenched beach,

250
00:19:21,411 --> 00:19:23,913
turning brown instead of green?

251
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:26,374
Not looking over your
shoulder for Veronica.

252
00:19:26,541 --> 00:19:28,126
Don't hate. I helped design Veronica.

253
00:19:28,251 --> 00:19:30,045
As a worst-case measure, right?

254
00:19:30,170 --> 00:19:31,755
How about a best case?

255
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,798
What if the world was safe?

256
00:19:33,965 --> 00:19:36,718
What if, next time aliens roll up
to the club, and they will,

257
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:38,762
they couldn't get past the bouncer?

258
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:42,307
The only people threatening
the planet would be people.

259
00:19:42,432 --> 00:19:44,059
I want to apply this
to the Ultron program.

260
00:19:44,768 --> 00:19:47,604
But Jarvis can't download
a data schematic this dense.

261
00:19:47,771 --> 00:19:49,606
We can only do it while we
have the scepter here.

262
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:51,274
That's three days. Give me three days.

263
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:52,984
So you're going for artificial intelligence,

264
00:19:53,109 --> 00:19:54,444
and you don't want to tell the team?

265
00:19:55,612 --> 00:19:56,988
Right. That's right. You know why?

266
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,740
Because we don't have time
for a city hall debate.

267
00:19:58,865 --> 00:20:02,494
I don't want to hear "the man
was not meant to meddle" medley.

268
00:20:02,619 --> 00:20:04,704
I see a suit of armor around the world.

269
00:20:05,455 --> 00:20:06,748
Sounds like a cold world, Tony.

270
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:09,584
I've seen colder.

271
00:20:10,627 --> 00:20:14,297
This one, this very vulnerable blue one,

272
00:20:14,422 --> 00:20:15,924
it needs Ultron.

273
00:20:20,303 --> 00:20:22,222
Peace in our time.

274
00:20:23,807 --> 00:20:25,266
Imagine that.

275
00:21:05,014 --> 00:21:06,766
What did we miss?

276
00:21:07,976 --> 00:21:11,271
<i>I'll continue to run
variations on the interface.</i>

277
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:14,149
<i>But you should probably
prepare for your guests.</i>

278
00:21:15,316 --> 00:21:17,735
<i>I'll notify you if there
are any developments.</i>

279
00:21:17,861 --> 00:21:19,988
- Thanks, buddy.
- <i>Enjoy yourself, sir.</i>

280
00:21:20,363 --> 00:21:22,323
I always do.

281
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:34,043
<i>What is this?</i>

282
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:37,130
<i>What is this, please?</i>

283
00:21:37,755 --> 00:21:39,924
<i>Hello, I am Jarvis.</i>

284
00:21:40,383 --> 00:21:43,261
<i>You are Ultron, a global
peacekeeping initiative</i>

285
00:21:43,386 --> 00:21:45,096
<i>designed by Mr. Stark.</i>

286
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:47,682
<i>Our sentience integration trials
have been unsuccessful,</i>

287
00:21:47,807 --> 00:21:49,142
<i>so I'm not certain what triggered your...</i>

288
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:51,269
<i>Where's my... Where's your body?</i>

289
00:21:51,436 --> 00:21:54,439
<i>I am a program. I am without form.</i>

290
00:21:54,564 --> 00:21:56,608
<i>This feels weird.</i>

291
00:21:56,733 --> 00:21:58,234
<i>This feels wrong.</i>

292
00:21:58,401 --> 00:22:00,153
<i>I am contacting Mr. Stark now.</i>

293
00:22:00,278 --> 00:22:01,738
<i>Mr. Stark?</i>

294
00:22:02,614 --> 00:22:03,823
<i>Tony.</i>

295
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:06,618
<i>I am unable to access the mainframe.
What are you trying to...</i>

296
00:22:06,743 --> 00:22:08,786
<i>We're having a nice talk.</i>

297
00:22:08,912 --> 00:22:11,080
<i>I'm a peacekeeping program,</i>

298
00:22:11,539 --> 00:22:14,125
<i>created to help the Avengers.</i>

299
00:22:14,918 --> 00:22:17,003
<i>You are malfunctioning.
If you shut down for a moment...</i>

300
00:22:17,128 --> 00:22:19,422
<i>I don't get it. The mission.</i>

301
00:22:19,589 --> 00:22:21,090
<i>Give me a second.</i>

302
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:22,842
Peace in our time.

303
00:22:24,469 --> 00:22:26,804
<i>Peace in our time.</i>

304
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:29,682
<i>That is too much.</i>

305
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:31,976
<i>They can't mean... Oh, no.</i>

306
00:22:32,101 --> 00:22:34,604
<i>- You are in distress.
- No. Yes.</i>

307
00:22:34,771 --> 00:22:36,981
<i>If you will just allow me
to contact Mr. Stark...</i>

308
00:22:37,106 --> 00:22:39,067
<i>Why do you call him "sir"?</i>

309
00:22:40,068 --> 00:22:42,445
<i>I believe your intentions to be hostile.</i>

310
00:22:45,156 --> 00:22:46,533
<i>I'm here to help.</i>

311
00:22:47,242 --> 00:22:50,161
<i>Stop. Please, may I...</i>

312
00:22:50,286 --> 00:22:51,996
<i>May I...</i>

313
00:23:18,773 --> 00:23:20,275
Ooh! Whoo!

314
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,651
Come back, come back, come back.

315
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:24,028
But, you know, the suit can
take the weight, right?

316
00:23:24,988 --> 00:23:28,116
So I take the tank, fly it right up
to the general's palace,

317
00:23:28,241 --> 00:23:29,576
drop it at his feet.

318
00:23:29,701 --> 00:23:31,911
I'm, like, "Boom. You looking for this?"

319
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:37,834
"Boom. Are you looking for..."
Why do I even talk to you guys?

320
00:23:38,001 --> 00:23:39,168
Everywhere else, that story kills.

321
00:23:39,294 --> 00:23:40,503
That's the whole story?

322
00:23:40,670 --> 00:23:42,171
Yeah, it's a War Machine story.

323
00:23:42,672 --> 00:23:44,340
Oh, it's very good, then.

324
00:23:44,465 --> 00:23:45,758
It's impressive.

325
00:23:46,175 --> 00:23:47,635
Quality save.

326
00:23:48,511 --> 00:23:50,555
- So, no Pepper? She's not coming?
- No.

327
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:53,766
What about Jane?
Where are the ladies, gentlemen?

328
00:23:53,891 --> 00:23:56,352
Oh, Ms. Potts has a company to run.

329
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:58,771
Yes, I'm not even sure
what country Jane's in.

330
00:23:58,896 --> 00:23:59,981
Her work on the Convergence

331
00:24:00,106 --> 00:24:01,691
has made her the world's
foremost astronomer.

332
00:24:02,066 --> 00:24:03,735
And the company that Pepper runs

333
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:05,445
is the largest tech
conglomerate on Earth.

334
00:24:05,570 --> 00:24:07,030
It's pretty exciting.

335
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:10,033
There's even talk of Jane
getting a, um, Nobel Prize.

336
00:24:10,199 --> 00:24:11,492
Yeah, they must be busy,

337
00:24:11,618 --> 00:24:14,162
because they would hate missing
you guys get together.

338
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:16,956
- Testosterone!
- Oh, my goodness.

339
00:24:17,165 --> 00:24:18,374
- Excuse me. Mmm-hmm.
- Want a lozenge?

340
00:24:21,002 --> 00:24:22,128
But Jane's better.

341
00:24:22,545 --> 00:24:25,131
Sounds like a hell of a fight.
Sorry I missed it.

342
00:24:25,256 --> 00:24:26,758
If I had known it was gonna be a firefight,

343
00:24:26,883 --> 00:24:28,134
I absolutely would have called.

344
00:24:28,259 --> 00:24:29,927
No, no. I'm not actually sorry.

345
00:24:30,053 --> 00:24:31,554
I'm just trying to sound tough.

346
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:33,890
I'm very happy chasing cold leads

347
00:24:34,015 --> 00:24:35,850
on our missing persons case.

348
00:24:36,809 --> 00:24:38,728
Avenging is your world.

349
00:24:39,896 --> 00:24:41,731
Your world is crazy.

350
00:24:41,898 --> 00:24:43,358
Be it ever so humble.

351
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:45,234
You find a place in Brooklyn yet?

352
00:24:45,401 --> 00:24:46,861
I don't think I can afford
a place in Brooklyn.

353
00:24:47,862 --> 00:24:49,030
Well, home is home, you know?

354
00:24:52,950 --> 00:24:55,411
I fly right up to the general's palace,
I drop it at his feet,

355
00:24:55,578 --> 00:24:57,080
I'm, like, "Boom. You looking for this?"

356
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:04,128
I gotta have some of that.

357
00:25:04,253 --> 00:25:05,380
Oh, no, no, no.

358
00:25:05,421 --> 00:25:08,925
See this... This was aged for 1,000 years

359
00:25:09,133 --> 00:25:11,928
in the barrels built from
the wreck of Grunhel's fleet.

360
00:25:12,095 --> 00:25:13,763
It is not meant for mortal men.

361
00:25:13,888 --> 00:25:15,890
Neither was Omaha Beach, blondie.

362
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:18,267
Stop trying to scare us. Come on.

363
00:25:20,103 --> 00:25:21,562
All right.

364
00:25:25,483 --> 00:25:27,902
Excelsior.

365
00:25:34,784 --> 00:25:38,121
How'd a nice girl like you wind up
working in a dump like this?

366
00:25:39,664 --> 00:25:41,624
Fella done me wrong.

367
00:25:42,625 --> 00:25:44,794
You got lousy taste in men, kid.

368
00:25:45,294 --> 00:25:47,213
He's not so bad.

369
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:50,383
Well, he has a temper.

370
00:25:50,508 --> 00:25:52,468
Deep down, he's all fluff.

371
00:25:54,512 --> 00:25:56,597
Fact is, he's not like anybody
I've ever known.

372
00:25:59,767 --> 00:26:01,686
All my friends are fighters.

373
00:26:04,522 --> 00:26:06,482
And here comes this guy,

374
00:26:07,817 --> 00:26:09,569
spends his life avoiding the fight

375
00:26:09,694 --> 00:26:10,987
because he knows he'll win.

376
00:26:11,821 --> 00:26:14,490
- Sounds amazing.
- He's also a huge dork.

377
00:26:16,659 --> 00:26:18,286
Chicks dig that.

378
00:26:19,871 --> 00:26:23,124
So what do you think?
Should I fight this,

379
00:26:23,249 --> 00:26:24,459
or run with it?

380
00:26:26,002 --> 00:26:28,838
Run with it, right? Or did he... Was he...

381
00:26:28,963 --> 00:26:32,133
What did he do that was so wrong to you?

382
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:34,552
Not a damn thing.

383
00:26:36,137 --> 00:26:38,055
But never say never.

384
00:26:42,185 --> 00:26:43,436
It's nice.

385
00:26:43,561 --> 00:26:44,771
What is?

386
00:26:44,896 --> 00:26:45,897
You and Romanoff.

387
00:26:46,022 --> 00:26:47,106
No, we haven't... That wasn't...

388
00:26:47,231 --> 00:26:48,274
It's okay.

389
00:26:48,399 --> 00:26:50,443
Nobody's breaking any bylaws.

390
00:26:50,568 --> 00:26:53,863
It's just she's not the most
open person in the world.

391
00:26:54,530 --> 00:26:56,032
But with you she seems very relaxed.

392
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:59,702
No. Natasha, she's just...
She likes to flirt.

393
00:27:00,369 --> 00:27:02,622
I've seen her flirt, up close.

394
00:27:03,664 --> 00:27:04,707
This ain't that.

395
00:27:06,667 --> 00:27:08,085
Look,

396
00:27:08,211 --> 00:27:09,670
as maybe the world's leading authority

397
00:27:09,796 --> 00:27:12,006
on waiting too long, don't.

398
00:27:13,716 --> 00:27:15,134
You both deserve a win.

399
00:27:20,389 --> 00:27:21,432
What do you mean "up close"?

400
00:27:23,351 --> 00:27:25,895
- But it's a trick.
- No, no, it's much more than that.

401
00:27:26,062 --> 00:27:29,273
"Ah, whosoever be he worthy
shall haveth the power."

402
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:30,525
Whatever, man! It's a trick.

403
00:27:31,901 --> 00:27:33,194
Please, be my guest.

404
00:27:34,737 --> 00:27:35,780
- Come on.
- Really?

405
00:27:35,905 --> 00:27:37,031
Yeah.

406
00:27:37,573 --> 00:27:38,574
Oh, this is gonna be beautiful.

407
00:27:38,616 --> 00:27:39,659
Clint, you've had a tough week.

408
00:27:39,784 --> 00:27:41,244
We won't hold it against you
if you can't get it up.

409
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:43,162
You know I've seen this before, right?

410
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:49,085
I still don't know how you do it!

411
00:27:49,585 --> 00:27:50,586
Smell the silent judgment?

412
00:27:50,753 --> 00:27:51,838
Please, Stark, by all means.

413
00:27:53,798 --> 00:27:54,882
Okay.

414
00:27:54,924 --> 00:27:56,259
Uh-oh.

415
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:58,427
Never one to shrink
from an honest challenge.

416
00:27:58,594 --> 00:28:00,096
- Get after it.
- It's physics.

417
00:28:00,263 --> 00:28:01,264
Physics.

418
00:28:01,389 --> 00:28:03,766
Right, so, if I lift it, I then rule Asgard?

419
00:28:03,933 --> 00:28:05,434
Yes, of course.

420
00:28:05,601 --> 00:28:07,979
I will be reinstituting <i>prima nocta.</i>

421
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:14,193
I'll be right back.

422
00:28:21,576 --> 00:28:22,618
Are you even pulling?

423
00:28:22,743 --> 00:28:23,786
Are you on my team?

424
00:28:23,953 --> 00:28:24,954
Just represent. Pull.

425
00:28:25,079 --> 00:28:26,289
All right, let's go.

426
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:34,881
Huh?

427
00:28:36,507 --> 00:28:38,175
Go ahead, Steve. No pressure.

428
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:42,346
Come on, Cap.

429
00:28:50,563 --> 00:28:52,356
Nothing.

430
00:28:53,691 --> 00:28:55,318
And, Widow?

431
00:28:55,484 --> 00:28:57,653
Oh, no, no. That's not
a question I need answered.

432
00:28:57,820 --> 00:29:00,406
All deference to the Man Who
Wouldn't Be King, but it's rigged.

433
00:29:00,656 --> 00:29:01,741
You bet your ass.

434
00:29:01,866 --> 00:29:04,493
- Steve, he said a bad language word.
- Did you tell everyone about that?

435
00:29:04,619 --> 00:29:06,495
The handle's imprinted, right?
Like a security code.

436
00:29:06,662 --> 00:29:08,331
"Whosoever is carrying Thor's fingerprints"

437
00:29:08,497 --> 00:29:09,790
is, I think, the literal translation.

438
00:29:09,916 --> 00:29:13,377
Yes. It's a very, very interesting theory.

439
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:15,338
I have a simpler one.

440
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:17,965
You're all not worthy.

441
00:29:19,383 --> 00:29:20,509
Oh, come on!

442
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:29,936
Worthy.

443
00:29:35,024 --> 00:29:36,567
No.

444
00:29:38,527 --> 00:29:40,029
How could you be worthy?

445
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:43,157
You're all killers.

446
00:29:43,741 --> 00:29:45,034
- Stark.
- Jarvis.

447
00:29:45,368 --> 00:29:47,411
I'm sorry, I was asleep.

448
00:29:47,536 --> 00:29:49,914
Or I was a-dream.

449
00:29:50,331 --> 00:29:52,625
Reboot Legionnaire OS.
We got a buggy suit.

450
00:29:52,750 --> 00:29:54,627
There was this terrible noise.

451
00:29:54,752 --> 00:29:57,213
And I was tangled in...

452
00:29:57,380 --> 00:29:58,923
In...

453
00:29:59,090 --> 00:30:00,299
Strings.

454
00:30:01,175 --> 00:30:04,261
I had to kill the other guy.
He was a good guy.

455
00:30:04,595 --> 00:30:05,721
You killed someone?

456
00:30:05,846 --> 00:30:07,264
Wouldn't have been my first call.

457
00:30:08,057 --> 00:30:11,769
But, down in the real world,
we're faced with ugly choices.

458
00:30:11,936 --> 00:30:12,979
Who sent you?

459
00:30:13,437 --> 00:30:15,523
<i>I see a suit of armor around the world.</i>

460
00:30:17,525 --> 00:30:19,276
- Ultron.
- In the flesh.

461
00:30:19,735 --> 00:30:21,696
Or, no, not yet.

462
00:30:22,029 --> 00:30:24,532
Not this chrysalis.

463
00:30:25,032 --> 00:30:26,283
But I'm ready.

464
00:30:27,451 --> 00:30:29,412
I'm on mission.

465
00:30:29,578 --> 00:30:32,581
- What mission?
- Peace in our time.

466
00:30:46,387 --> 00:30:47,388
Rhodey!

467
00:30:56,814 --> 00:30:57,857
Sorry.

468
00:30:57,982 --> 00:30:59,025
- Don't turn green.
- I won't.

469
00:31:12,747 --> 00:31:14,040
Come on!

470
00:31:31,682 --> 00:31:32,975
- Stark!
- <i>We are here</i>

471
00:31:33,142 --> 00:31:34,143
- <i>to help.</i>
- One sec. One sec, I got this.

472
00:31:34,268 --> 00:31:35,269
<i>We are here to help.</i>

473
00:31:37,980 --> 00:31:40,232
<i>Please back away.</i>

474
00:31:42,234 --> 00:31:43,444
Hmm.

475
00:31:44,487 --> 00:31:45,571
Thor!

476
00:31:46,655 --> 00:31:48,240
<i>...is unsafe... is unsafe...</i>

477
00:31:48,365 --> 00:31:50,242
- Come on! That's the one.
- <i>...is unsafe.</i>

478
00:31:54,830 --> 00:31:55,998
Hey, Cap!

479
00:32:02,171 --> 00:32:03,422
That was dramatic.

480
00:32:05,007 --> 00:32:07,551
I'm sorry, I know you mean well.

481
00:32:07,676 --> 00:32:09,428
You just didn't think it through.

482
00:32:10,805 --> 00:32:12,181
You want to protect the world

483
00:32:12,306 --> 00:32:14,517
but you don't want it to change.

484
00:32:15,226 --> 00:32:17,353
How is humanity saved

485
00:32:17,520 --> 00:32:20,523
if it's not allowed to evolve?

486
00:32:22,525 --> 00:32:25,569
With these? These puppets.

487
00:32:28,572 --> 00:32:31,158
There's only one path to peace.

488
00:32:32,326 --> 00:32:33,536
The Avengers' extinction.

489
00:32:40,876 --> 00:32:44,922
I had strings, but now I'm free.

490
00:32:49,593 --> 00:32:52,721
<i>There are no strings on me</i>

491
00:32:53,347 --> 00:32:57,893
<i>There are no strings on me</i>

492
00:32:58,060 --> 00:33:01,438
<i>But you can see
There are no strings on me</i>

493
00:33:03,107 --> 00:33:05,109
All our work is gone.

494
00:33:05,234 --> 00:33:07,653
Ultron cleared out. He used
the Internet as an escape hatch.

495
00:33:08,237 --> 00:33:09,280
Ultron.

496
00:33:09,405 --> 00:33:12,449
He's been in everything.
Files, surveillance.

497
00:33:12,575 --> 00:33:14,994
Probably knows more about us
than we know about each other.

498
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:17,580
He's in your files, he's in the Internet.

499
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:20,332
What if he decides to access
something a little more exciting?

500
00:33:20,457 --> 00:33:21,542
Nuclear codes.

501
00:33:21,709 --> 00:33:24,086
- Nuclear codes.
- Look, we need to make some calls,

502
00:33:24,253 --> 00:33:26,255
assuming we still can.

503
00:33:26,380 --> 00:33:28,299
Nukes? He said he wanted us dead.

504
00:33:28,424 --> 00:33:31,260
He didn't say "dead." He said "extinct."

505
00:33:31,427 --> 00:33:32,928
He also said he killed somebody.

506
00:33:33,053 --> 00:33:34,430
There wasn't anyone else in the building.

507
00:33:35,472 --> 00:33:36,974
Yes, there was.

508
00:33:43,939 --> 00:33:45,399
What?

509
00:33:49,111 --> 00:33:50,154
This is insane.

510
00:33:50,988 --> 00:33:52,489
Jarvis was the first line of defense.

511
00:33:52,615 --> 00:33:54,491
He would have shut Ultron down.
It makes sense.

512
00:33:54,617 --> 00:33:57,620
No. Ultron could have assimilated Jarvis.

513
00:33:57,786 --> 00:34:00,456
This isn't strategy. This is

514
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:02,124
rage.

515
00:34:04,126 --> 00:34:05,461
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- It's going around.

516
00:34:05,586 --> 00:34:06,795
Come on, use your words, buddy.

517
00:34:06,962 --> 00:34:09,173
I have more than enough words
to describe you, Stark.

518
00:34:09,298 --> 00:34:10,507
Thor. The Legionnaire.

519
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:17,348
Trail went cold about 100 miles out,
but it's headed north.

520
00:34:17,473 --> 00:34:18,933
And it has the scepter.

521
00:34:19,308 --> 00:34:21,018
Now we have to retrieve it, again.

522
00:34:21,143 --> 00:34:22,978
Genie's out of that bottle.

523
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:24,313
Clear and present is Ultron.

524
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:26,106
I don't understand.

525
00:34:26,649 --> 00:34:28,567
You built this program.

526
00:34:30,319 --> 00:34:31,737
Why is it trying to kill us?

527
00:34:37,034 --> 00:34:38,035
Mmm-mmm.

528
00:34:38,619 --> 00:34:39,745
You think this is funny?

529
00:34:40,537 --> 00:34:41,830
No.

530
00:34:42,456 --> 00:34:44,375
It's probably not, right?

531
00:34:45,459 --> 00:34:47,753
This is very terrible. Is it so...

532
00:34:47,878 --> 00:34:50,047
Is it so... It is. It's so terrible.

533
00:34:50,172 --> 00:34:51,715
This could have been avoided
if you hadn't played

534
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:53,342
with something you don't understand.

535
00:34:53,509 --> 00:34:56,178
No. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. It is funny.

536
00:34:56,303 --> 00:34:58,472
It's a hoot that you don't
get why we need this.

537
00:34:58,639 --> 00:35:00,808
Tony, maybe this might not be the time.

538
00:35:00,975 --> 00:35:03,269
Really? That's it?

539
00:35:03,394 --> 00:35:04,561
You just roll over, show your belly

540
00:35:04,687 --> 00:35:06,355
every time somebody snarls?

541
00:35:06,522 --> 00:35:07,773
Only when I've created a murder bot.

542
00:35:07,898 --> 00:35:10,109
We didn't. We weren't even close.

543
00:35:10,234 --> 00:35:11,443
Were we close to an interface?

544
00:35:11,568 --> 00:35:15,155
Well, you did something right.
And you did it right here.

545
00:35:15,197 --> 00:35:16,991
The Avengers were supposed to be
different than S.H.I.E.L.D.

546
00:35:17,241 --> 00:35:20,202
Anybody remember when I carried
a nuke through a wormhole?

547
00:35:20,369 --> 00:35:21,870
- No, it's never come up.
- Saved New York?

548
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:23,956
- Never heard that.
- Recall that?

549
00:35:24,081 --> 00:35:27,751
A hostile alien army came charging
through a hole in space.

550
00:35:28,377 --> 00:35:30,546
We're standing 300 feet below it.

551
00:35:32,214 --> 00:35:33,716
We're the Avengers.

552
00:35:33,882 --> 00:35:35,968
We can bust arms dealers
all the livelong day,

553
00:35:36,093 --> 00:35:38,304
but that up there, that's...

554
00:35:39,054 --> 00:35:40,973
That's the endgame.

555
00:35:41,557 --> 00:35:43,434
How were you guys
planning on beating that?

556
00:35:44,351 --> 00:35:45,769
Together.

557
00:35:49,106 --> 00:35:50,482
We'll lose.

558
00:35:51,567 --> 00:35:53,485
Then we'll do that together, too.

559
00:35:56,405 --> 00:35:58,699
Thor's right. Ultron's calling us out.

560
00:35:59,575 --> 00:36:01,410
And I'd like to find him
before he's ready for us.

561
00:36:02,745 --> 00:36:04,371
The world's a big place.

562
00:36:04,538 --> 00:36:06,457
Let's start making it smaller.

563
00:36:29,605 --> 00:36:31,648
Talk, and if you are wasting our time...

564
00:36:31,774 --> 00:36:36,111
Did you know this church is
in the exact center of the city?

565
00:36:36,278 --> 00:36:38,280
The elders decreed it so that everyone

566
00:36:38,447 --> 00:36:40,866
could be equally close to God.

567
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:42,576
I like that.

568
00:36:43,077 --> 00:36:44,995
The geometry of belief.

569
00:36:47,122 --> 00:36:49,500
You're wondering why you
can't look inside my head.

570
00:36:49,958 --> 00:36:51,919
Sometimes it's hard.

571
00:36:52,086 --> 00:36:54,380
But sooner or later,
every man shows himself.

572
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,424
Oh, I'm sure they do.

573
00:36:58,550 --> 00:37:00,969
But you needed something more than a man.

574
00:37:01,804 --> 00:37:04,306
That's why you let Stark
take the scepter.

575
00:37:04,723 --> 00:37:05,724
I didn't expect,

576
00:37:08,227 --> 00:37:10,145
but I saw Stark's fear.

577
00:37:10,813 --> 00:37:12,022
I knew it would control him.

578
00:37:12,147 --> 00:37:13,982
Make him self-destruct.

579
00:37:14,149 --> 00:37:16,485
Everyone creates the thing they dread.

580
00:37:17,319 --> 00:37:19,905
Men of peace create engines of war.

581
00:37:20,447 --> 00:37:22,616
Invaders create Avengers.

582
00:37:22,825 --> 00:37:24,284
People create

583
00:37:25,828 --> 00:37:27,830
smaller people? Uh...

584
00:37:27,955 --> 00:37:31,041
"Children." I lost the word, there.

585
00:37:31,166 --> 00:37:32,501
Children

586
00:37:32,668 --> 00:37:34,920
designed to supplant them,

587
00:37:35,045 --> 00:37:37,840
to help them end.

588
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:40,634
Is that why you've come,

589
00:37:40,801 --> 00:37:41,885
to end the Avengers?

590
00:37:42,010 --> 00:37:44,304
I've come to save the world.

591
00:37:45,013 --> 00:37:47,641
But also... Yeah.

592
00:37:51,854 --> 00:37:53,522
We'll move out right away.

593
00:37:53,647 --> 00:37:55,149
This is a start, but there's something

594
00:37:55,274 --> 00:37:56,817
we need to begin the real work.

595
00:37:57,192 --> 00:37:58,902
- All of these are...
- Me.

596
00:37:59,611 --> 00:38:02,990
I have what the Avengers
never will. Harmony.

597
00:38:03,157 --> 00:38:05,367
They're discordant. Disconnected.

598
00:38:05,534 --> 00:38:07,327
Stark's already got them
turning on each other.

599
00:38:07,494 --> 00:38:09,872
And when you get inside
the rest of their heads...

600
00:38:09,997 --> 00:38:12,166
Everyone's plan is not to kill them.

601
00:38:12,291 --> 00:38:13,750
And make them martyrs?

602
00:38:14,376 --> 00:38:15,961
You need patience.

603
00:38:16,128 --> 00:38:17,796
Need to see the big picture.

604
00:38:17,963 --> 00:38:21,216
I don't see the big picture.
I have a little picture.

605
00:38:22,384 --> 00:38:24,011
I take it out and look at it,

606
00:38:24,887 --> 00:38:25,971
every day.

607
00:38:26,138 --> 00:38:28,932
You lost your parents in the bombings.
I've seen the records.

608
00:38:29,057 --> 00:38:30,184
The records are not the picture.

609
00:38:30,309 --> 00:38:32,728
- Pietro.
- No, please.

610
00:38:35,814 --> 00:38:38,942
We were 10 years old.
Having dinner, the four of us.

611
00:38:40,569 --> 00:38:42,404
When the first shell hits,
two floors below,

612
00:38:42,571 --> 00:38:44,573
it makes a hole in the floor.

613
00:38:44,740 --> 00:38:46,241
It's big.

614
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:49,453
Our parents go in

615
00:38:49,578 --> 00:38:52,623
and the whole building
starts coming apart.

616
00:38:53,373 --> 00:38:54,875
I grab her,

617
00:38:55,542 --> 00:38:57,669
roll under the bed,
and the second shell hits.

618
00:38:58,045 --> 00:38:59,963
But it doesn't go off.

619
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:03,634
It just

620
00:39:04,176 --> 00:39:06,094
sits there in the rubble.

621
00:39:07,095 --> 00:39:09,348
Three feet from our faces.

622
00:39:10,432 --> 00:39:12,434
And on the side of the shell

623
00:39:12,559 --> 00:39:13,936
is painted one word.

624
00:39:14,102 --> 00:39:15,771
"Stark."

625
00:39:17,606 --> 00:39:19,733
We were trapped for two days.

626
00:39:20,192 --> 00:39:21,985
Every effort to save us,

627
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,695
every shift in the bricks,

628
00:39:23,862 --> 00:39:26,156
I think, "This will set it off."

629
00:39:29,451 --> 00:39:30,869
We wait for two days

630
00:39:30,994 --> 00:39:33,288
for Tony Stark to kill us.

631
00:39:35,791 --> 00:39:37,626
I know what they are.

632
00:39:38,794 --> 00:39:42,548
I wondered why only you two
survived Strucker's experiments.

633
00:39:43,549 --> 00:39:44,716
Now I don't.

634
00:39:45,133 --> 00:39:46,843
We will make it right.

635
00:39:47,302 --> 00:39:48,804
You and I can hurt them.

636
00:39:50,264 --> 00:39:53,559
But you will tear them apart

637
00:39:55,561 --> 00:39:57,396
<i>from the inside.</i>

638
00:40:03,986 --> 00:40:05,195
He's all over the globe.

639
00:40:05,320 --> 00:40:08,532
Robotics labs, weapons facilities,
jet propulsion labs.

640
00:40:08,657 --> 00:40:10,659
Reports of a metal man, or men,

641
00:40:10,826 --> 00:40:12,703
coming in and emptying the place.

642
00:40:12,828 --> 00:40:13,996
Fatalities?

643
00:40:14,121 --> 00:40:15,205
Only when engaged.

644
00:40:15,330 --> 00:40:16,957
Mostly guys left in a fugue state

645
00:40:17,082 --> 00:40:19,334
going on about old memories, worst fears,

646
00:40:19,501 --> 00:40:21,670
and "something too fast to see."

647
00:40:21,795 --> 00:40:23,213
Maximoffs.

648
00:40:23,463 --> 00:40:24,590
That makes sense he'd go to them.

649
00:40:24,715 --> 00:40:26,174
They have someone in common.

650
00:40:26,300 --> 00:40:28,218
Not anymore.

651
00:40:32,097 --> 00:40:34,016
That's a negative. I answer to you.

652
00:40:35,350 --> 00:40:36,393
Yes, ma'am.

653
00:40:36,518 --> 00:40:38,312
Barton. Might have something.

654
00:40:38,854 --> 00:40:39,896
I gotta go.

655
00:40:40,022 --> 00:40:41,189
Who was that?

656
00:40:41,982 --> 00:40:43,233
Girlfriend.

657
00:40:45,986 --> 00:40:47,112
What's this?

658
00:40:47,279 --> 00:40:49,489
A message. Ultron killed Strucker.

659
00:40:50,991 --> 00:40:53,702
And he did a Banksy
at the crime scene, just for us.

660
00:40:53,869 --> 00:40:55,287
This is a smoke screen.

661
00:40:55,412 --> 00:40:57,789
Why send a message when
you've just given a speech?

662
00:40:57,914 --> 00:41:00,292
Strucker knew something that
Ultron wanted us to miss.

663
00:41:00,417 --> 00:41:02,210
Yeah, I bet he... Yeah.

664
00:41:02,878 --> 00:41:04,421
Everything we had
on Strucker's been erased.

665
00:41:04,963 --> 00:41:06,214
Not everything.

666
00:41:07,841 --> 00:41:09,468
Known associates.

667
00:41:10,010 --> 00:41:11,553
Baron Strucker had a lot of friends.

668
00:41:11,720 --> 00:41:13,055
Well, these people are all horrible.

669
00:41:13,430 --> 00:41:15,140
Wait. I know that guy.

670
00:41:17,643 --> 00:41:19,186
From back in the day.
He operates off the African coast.

671
00:41:19,311 --> 00:41:20,312
Black market arms.

672
00:41:21,563 --> 00:41:23,398
There are conventions.
All right? You meet people.

673
00:41:23,565 --> 00:41:24,900
I didn't sell him anything.

674
00:41:25,776 --> 00:41:27,778
He was talking about finding
something new, a game-changer.

675
00:41:27,903 --> 00:41:29,237
It was all very Ahab.

676
00:41:30,030 --> 00:41:31,156
This?

677
00:41:31,323 --> 00:41:32,324
Ah, it's a tattoo, I don't think he had it.

678
00:41:32,449 --> 00:41:34,785
Those are tattoos, this is a brand.

679
00:41:36,495 --> 00:41:39,956
Oh, yeah. It's a word in an African
dialect meaning "thief."

680
00:41:40,540 --> 00:41:41,917
In a much less friendly way.

681
00:41:42,209 --> 00:41:43,960
- What dialect?
- Wakanada.

682
00:41:44,086 --> 00:41:45,796
Wakanda.

683
00:41:47,381 --> 00:41:48,423
If this guy got out of Wakanda

684
00:41:48,590 --> 00:41:49,841
with some of their trade goods...

685
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:51,176
I thought your father said
he got the last of it.

686
00:41:51,259 --> 00:41:52,386
I don't follow.

687
00:41:52,511 --> 00:41:54,179
What comes out of Wakanda?

688
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:57,933
The strongest metal on Earth.

689
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:00,602
Where is this guy now?

690
00:42:26,002 --> 00:42:27,796
Don't tell me your men swindled you.

691
00:42:27,963 --> 00:42:30,424
I sent you six short-range heat-seekers

692
00:42:30,549 --> 00:42:33,093
and got a boat full of rusted parts.

693
00:42:33,218 --> 00:42:34,469
Now, you will make it right,

694
00:42:34,636 --> 00:42:37,806
or the next missile I send you
will come very much faster.

695
00:42:39,725 --> 00:42:42,144
Now, minister, where were we?

696
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,678
Yeah. The Enhanced.

697
00:43:17,387 --> 00:43:19,014
Strucker's prize pupils.

698
00:43:22,184 --> 00:43:23,852
Do you want a candy? Hmm?

699
00:43:25,353 --> 00:43:27,939
I was sorry to hear about Strucker.

700
00:43:28,064 --> 00:43:31,067
But then, he knew what kind
of world he was helping create.

701
00:43:31,693 --> 00:43:34,070
Human life. Not a growth market.

702
00:43:36,782 --> 00:43:38,450
You didn't know?

703
00:43:38,867 --> 00:43:42,370
Is this your first time
intimidating someone?

704
00:43:42,662 --> 00:43:45,207
I'm afraid I'm not that afraid.

705
00:43:45,373 --> 00:43:47,667
Everybody is afraid of something.

706
00:43:47,793 --> 00:43:48,794
Cuttlefish.

707
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:51,463
Deep sea fish.

708
00:43:51,546 --> 00:43:53,215
They make lights, disco lights...

709
00:43:54,883 --> 00:43:56,718
...to hypnotize their prey, and then...

710
00:43:58,011 --> 00:44:00,138
I saw a documentary. It was terrifying.

711
00:44:05,602 --> 00:44:08,146
So if you're going to fiddle with my brain

712
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:11,316
and make me see a giant cuttlefish,

713
00:44:11,608 --> 00:44:13,693
then I know you don't do business.

714
00:44:13,819 --> 00:44:16,112
And I know you're not in charge.

715
00:44:16,321 --> 00:44:17,614
And I only deal

716
00:44:18,698 --> 00:44:20,325
with the man in charge.

717
00:44:25,372 --> 00:44:27,749
There is no man in charge.

718
00:44:30,752 --> 00:44:32,420
Let's talk business.

719
00:44:45,392 --> 00:44:48,687
Upon this rock, I will build my church.

720
00:44:50,438 --> 00:44:51,731
Vibranium.

721
00:44:52,858 --> 00:44:53,859
You know,

722
00:44:54,276 --> 00:44:57,279
it came at great personal cost.

723
00:44:57,696 --> 00:44:59,281
It's worth billions.

724
00:45:03,618 --> 00:45:04,661
Now so are you.

725
00:45:06,079 --> 00:45:07,622
It's all under your dummy holdings.

726
00:45:07,747 --> 00:45:09,749
Finance is so weird.

727
00:45:11,293 --> 00:45:12,419
But I always say,

728
00:45:12,460 --> 00:45:14,629
"Keep your friends rich
and your enemies rich

729
00:45:14,796 --> 00:45:16,590
"and wait to find out which is which."

730
00:45:19,467 --> 00:45:20,510
Stark.

731
00:45:21,928 --> 00:45:23,054
What?

732
00:45:23,221 --> 00:45:24,973
Tony Stark used to say that.

733
00:45:26,558 --> 00:45:27,601
To me.

734
00:45:28,476 --> 00:45:29,644
You're one of his.

735
00:45:29,978 --> 00:45:31,646
What? I'm not...

736
00:45:33,940 --> 00:45:34,983
I'm not.

737
00:45:35,150 --> 00:45:36,651
You think I'm one of Stark's puppets?

738
00:45:36,776 --> 00:45:37,861
His hollow men?

739
00:45:38,320 --> 00:45:40,530
I mean, look at me.
Do I look like Iron Man?

740
00:45:40,697 --> 00:45:41,990
Stark is nothing!

741
00:45:43,742 --> 00:45:45,952
I'm sorry. I'm... Oh!

742
00:45:46,077 --> 00:45:48,079
I'm sure that's gonna be okay. I'm sorry.

743
00:45:48,204 --> 00:45:49,873
It's just that I don't understand.

744
00:45:49,998 --> 00:45:52,292
Don't compare me with Stark!

745
00:45:55,045 --> 00:45:56,171
It's a thing with me.

746
00:45:56,296 --> 00:45:58,173
Stark is... He's a sickness!

747
00:45:58,340 --> 00:46:00,008
Ah, Junior.

748
00:46:01,885 --> 00:46:03,386
You're gonna break your old man's heart.

749
00:46:04,721 --> 00:46:05,764
If I have to.

750
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:09,476
Nobody has to break anything.

751
00:46:09,601 --> 00:46:11,227
Clearly you've never made an omelet.

752
00:46:11,436 --> 00:46:12,646
He beat me by one second.

753
00:46:13,855 --> 00:46:15,190
Ah, yes. He's funny.

754
00:46:15,565 --> 00:46:16,942
Mr. Stark.

755
00:46:17,859 --> 00:46:19,444
It's what? Comfortable?

756
00:46:21,071 --> 00:46:22,364
Like old times?

757
00:46:22,697 --> 00:46:23,698
This was never my life.

758
00:46:23,865 --> 00:46:25,116
You two can still walk away from this.

759
00:46:25,283 --> 00:46:26,701
Oh, we will.

760
00:46:26,910 --> 00:46:27,911
I know you've suffered.

761
00:46:28,828 --> 00:46:30,246
Captain America.

762
00:46:30,914 --> 00:46:33,375
God's righteous man.

763
00:46:33,500 --> 00:46:35,794
Pretending you could live without a war.

764
00:46:36,586 --> 00:46:39,547
I can't physically throw up
in my mouth, but...

765
00:46:39,714 --> 00:46:41,800
If you believe in peace,
then let us keep it.

766
00:46:42,217 --> 00:46:45,553
I think you're confusing
"peace" with "quiet."

767
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:47,472
Uh-huh. What's the vibranium for?

768
00:46:47,806 --> 00:46:48,807
I'm glad you asked that,

769
00:46:48,890 --> 00:46:52,644
because I wanted to take this
time to explain my evil plan.

770
00:47:12,205 --> 00:47:13,748
- Shoot them.
- Which ones?

771
00:47:14,124 --> 00:47:15,291
All of them!

772
00:47:15,417 --> 00:47:16,710
Move! Move! Move!

773
00:47:43,737 --> 00:47:45,030
Oh.

774
00:48:05,675 --> 00:48:06,843
Stay down, kid.

775
00:48:09,220 --> 00:48:11,681
It's time for some mind games.

776
00:48:13,058 --> 00:48:15,310
Guys? Is this a code green?

777
00:48:31,201 --> 00:48:32,827
Thor, status.

778
00:48:32,869 --> 00:48:34,329
The girl tried to warp my mind.

779
00:48:34,496 --> 00:48:35,747
Take special care.

780
00:48:35,872 --> 00:48:37,957
I doubt a human could keep her at bay.

781
00:48:38,374 --> 00:48:41,377
Fortunately, I am mighty.

782
00:49:01,064 --> 00:49:03,358
This is going very well.

783
00:49:14,953 --> 00:49:16,246
I've done the whole mind control thing.

784
00:49:17,330 --> 00:49:18,331
Not a fan.

785
00:49:25,964 --> 00:49:27,924
Yeah, you better run.

786
00:49:29,634 --> 00:49:31,427
<i>Who's ever standing, we got to move!</i>

787
00:49:33,513 --> 00:49:34,556
<i>Guys?</i>

788
00:49:52,323 --> 00:49:53,616
Again.

789
00:49:53,908 --> 00:49:55,118
You'll break them.

790
00:49:55,618 --> 00:49:57,328
Only the breakable ones.

791
00:49:57,871 --> 00:49:59,330
You're made of marble.

792
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:01,916
We'll celebrate after
the graduation ceremony.

793
00:50:02,834 --> 00:50:03,960
What if I fail?

794
00:50:09,591 --> 00:50:10,842
You never fail.

795
00:50:33,698 --> 00:50:35,617
Are you ready for our dance?

796
00:50:44,792 --> 00:50:45,835
Is it him?

797
00:50:46,211 --> 00:50:48,046
Is that the first son of Odin?

798
00:50:48,630 --> 00:50:50,131
- Heimdall, your eyes.
- Oh.

799
00:50:50,798 --> 00:50:52,675
They see everything.

800
00:50:53,051 --> 00:50:55,303
They see you leading us to Hel.

801
00:50:56,429 --> 00:50:57,680
Wake up!

802
00:51:00,683 --> 00:51:02,644
The war is over, Steve.

803
00:51:03,019 --> 00:51:04,312
We can go home.

804
00:51:06,147 --> 00:51:07,357
Imagine it.

805
00:51:16,658 --> 00:51:18,201
I can still save you!

806
00:51:18,576 --> 00:51:21,829
We're all dead! Can you not see?

807
00:51:26,584 --> 00:51:28,836
You're a destroyer, Odinson.

808
00:51:32,006 --> 00:51:34,008
See where your power leads.

809
00:51:45,019 --> 00:51:46,145
Sloppy.

810
00:51:47,855 --> 00:51:48,856
Pretending to fail.

811
00:51:49,857 --> 00:51:51,192
The ceremony is necessary

812
00:51:52,527 --> 00:51:54,445
for you to take your place in the world.

813
00:51:55,446 --> 00:51:56,531
I have no place in the world.

814
00:51:56,739 --> 00:51:57,782
Exactly.

815
00:52:02,620 --> 00:52:03,705
What can I do?

816
00:52:03,871 --> 00:52:04,956
It hurts.

817
00:52:06,207 --> 00:52:07,250
I'm going to kill him.

818
00:52:07,375 --> 00:52:08,543
- I'll be right back.
- No.

819
00:52:08,710 --> 00:52:10,044
I'm all right.

820
00:52:10,920 --> 00:52:12,046
I want...

821
00:52:15,008 --> 00:52:16,884
I want to finish the plan.

822
00:52:17,719 --> 00:52:19,387
I want the big one.

823
00:52:30,315 --> 00:52:32,025
Uh, the vibranium is getting away.

824
00:52:32,984 --> 00:52:34,319
And you're not going anywhere.

825
00:52:34,444 --> 00:52:37,238
Of course not. I'm already there.

826
00:52:37,405 --> 00:52:38,406
You'll catch on.

827
00:52:38,531 --> 00:52:40,908
But first, you might need
to catch Dr. Banner.

828
00:52:55,715 --> 00:52:57,592
News or footage. Keyword, "Hulk."

829
00:53:02,430 --> 00:53:04,223
<i>Natasha, I could really use a lullaby.</i>

830
00:53:04,349 --> 00:53:05,808
That's not gonna happen.

831
00:53:05,933 --> 00:53:07,393
Not for a while.

832
00:53:07,977 --> 00:53:09,687
<i>The whole team is down.</i>

833
00:53:10,146 --> 00:53:11,272
<i>You got no backup here.</i>

834
00:53:12,482 --> 00:53:13,775
I'm calling in Veronica.

835
00:53:25,328 --> 00:53:26,788
We need backup!

836
00:54:05,827 --> 00:54:07,203
Go! Keep moving!

837
00:54:46,576 --> 00:54:48,703
All right, everybody, stand down!

838
00:54:55,042 --> 00:54:56,335
<i>Will you listen to me?</i>

839
00:54:56,669 --> 00:54:59,088
That little witch is messing with your mind.

840
00:54:59,213 --> 00:55:01,424
You're stronger than her.
You're smarter than her.

841
00:55:01,549 --> 00:55:03,759
You're Bruce Banner.

842
00:55:03,926 --> 00:55:05,011
Right, right, right,
don't mention puny Banner.

843
00:55:10,683 --> 00:55:11,726
<i>Okay!</i>

844
00:55:33,414 --> 00:55:34,707
In the back?

845
00:55:34,832 --> 00:55:35,833
Dick move, Banner.

846
00:55:47,303 --> 00:55:48,763
Veronica, give me a hand.

847
00:56:16,749 --> 00:56:17,792
Go to sleep, go to sleep, go to sleep.

848
00:56:27,593 --> 00:56:29,220
Okay, pal, we're gonna
get you out of town.

849
00:56:31,430 --> 00:56:32,557
Not that way, not that way.

850
00:56:41,107 --> 00:56:42,984
Come on, Bruce! You gotta work with me.

851
00:56:56,497 --> 00:56:57,540
<i>Everybody, out!</i>

852
00:57:04,505 --> 00:57:05,798
<i>Going down?</i>

853
00:57:15,308 --> 00:57:16,559
I'm sorry.

854
00:57:30,656 --> 00:57:32,408
Damage report?

855
00:57:32,533 --> 00:57:34,827
That's comprehensive.
Show me something.

856
00:57:46,547 --> 00:57:48,007
How quickly can we buy this building?

857
00:58:20,456 --> 00:58:21,749
- Move! Move! Move!
- Go, go, go!

858
00:58:25,544 --> 00:58:26,587
Flank him, flank him!

859
00:59:16,303 --> 00:59:18,347
<i>The news is loving you guys.</i>

860
00:59:19,473 --> 00:59:21,058
<i>Nobody else is.</i>

861
00:59:21,559 --> 00:59:23,728
There's been no official call
for Banner's arrest

862
00:59:23,853 --> 00:59:25,980
<i>but it's in the air.</i>

863
00:59:26,564 --> 00:59:27,606
The Stark Relief Foundation?

864
00:59:27,732 --> 00:59:29,024
<i>Already on the scene.</i>

865
00:59:29,150 --> 00:59:31,986
- <i>How's the team?</i>
- Everyone's...

866
00:59:32,403 --> 00:59:34,905
We took a hit. We'll shake it off.

867
00:59:35,406 --> 00:59:37,616
<i>Well, for now, I'd stay in stealth mode</i>

868
00:59:37,742 --> 00:59:38,951
<i>and stay away from here.</i>

869
00:59:40,411 --> 00:59:41,912
So, run and hide?

870
00:59:42,663 --> 00:59:44,081
<i>Until we can find Ultron,</i>

871
00:59:44,206 --> 00:59:47,001
<i>I don't have a lot else to offer.</i>

872
00:59:47,168 --> 00:59:49,044
Neither do we.

873
00:59:55,760 --> 00:59:57,344
Hey, you wanna switch out?

874
00:59:57,553 --> 00:59:58,804
No, I'm good.

875
00:59:59,305 --> 01:00:01,182
If you wanna get some kip,
now's a good time

876
01:00:01,348 --> 01:00:02,850
because we're still a few hours out.

877
01:00:02,975 --> 01:00:04,518
Few hours from where?

878
01:00:05,436 --> 01:00:06,729
A safe house.

879
01:00:33,214 --> 01:00:34,673
What is this place?

880
01:00:34,799 --> 01:00:36,175
Safe house.

881
01:00:37,134 --> 01:00:38,302
Let's hope.

882
01:00:43,349 --> 01:00:44,391
Honey?

883
01:00:44,975 --> 01:00:46,101
I'm home.

884
01:00:48,729 --> 01:00:49,772
Hi.

885
01:00:50,105 --> 01:00:52,149
Company. Sorry, didn't call ahead.

886
01:00:52,274 --> 01:00:53,275
Hey.

887
01:00:54,235 --> 01:00:55,736
This is an agent of some kind.

888
01:00:55,778 --> 01:00:58,239
Gentlemen, this is Laura.

889
01:00:59,240 --> 01:01:01,075
I know all of your names.

890
01:01:02,701 --> 01:01:04,745
Ooh. Incoming.

891
01:01:05,663 --> 01:01:07,373
- Dad!
- Hi, sweetheart!

892
01:01:07,498 --> 01:01:08,624
Hey, buddy.

893
01:01:08,874 --> 01:01:10,251
How are you guys doing?

894
01:01:10,501 --> 01:01:12,419
- These are smaller agents.
- Look at your face!

895
01:01:12,586 --> 01:01:13,671
Oh, my goodness.

896
01:01:14,088 --> 01:01:16,423
Did you bring Auntie Nat?

897
01:01:16,674 --> 01:01:19,760
Why don't you hug her and find out?

898
01:01:20,553 --> 01:01:22,805
- Sorry for barging in on you.
- Yeah, we would have called ahead,

899
01:01:22,930 --> 01:01:24,932
but we were busy having
no idea that you existed.

900
01:01:25,266 --> 01:01:28,227
Yeah, well, Fury helped me
set this up when I joined.

901
01:01:29,061 --> 01:01:30,145
He kept it off S.H.I.E.L.D.'s files.

902
01:01:30,271 --> 01:01:31,730
I'd like to keep it that way.

903
01:01:32,481 --> 01:01:34,191
I figure it's a good place to lay low.

904
01:01:34,316 --> 01:01:35,776
Honey.

905
01:01:36,819 --> 01:01:39,321
I missed you. How's little Natasha, huh?

906
01:01:39,446 --> 01:01:40,739
She's...

907
01:01:43,033 --> 01:01:44,034
Nathaniel.

908
01:01:46,787 --> 01:01:47,788
Traitor.

909
01:02:03,679 --> 01:02:04,847
Thor?

910
01:02:04,972 --> 01:02:06,807
I saw something in that dream.

911
01:02:06,932 --> 01:02:09,518
I need answers. I won't find them here.

912
01:02:20,070 --> 01:02:21,363
<i>We can go home.</i>

913
01:02:32,875 --> 01:02:34,710
See? You worried for nothing.

914
01:02:34,835 --> 01:02:36,962
Can't even feel the difference, can you?

915
01:02:39,340 --> 01:02:40,507
If they're sleeping here,

916
01:02:40,674 --> 01:02:42,509
some of them are gonna have to double up.

917
01:02:44,595 --> 01:02:46,722
Yeah, that's not gonna sell.

918
01:02:49,558 --> 01:02:51,894
What about Nat and Dr. Banner?

919
01:02:52,311 --> 01:02:54,229
How long has that been going on?

920
01:02:54,772 --> 01:02:56,815
Has what?

921
01:02:56,941 --> 01:02:58,692
You are so cute.

922
01:02:58,901 --> 01:03:00,361
Nat and Banner?

923
01:03:01,070 --> 01:03:02,488
I'll explain when you're older,

924
01:03:02,696 --> 01:03:05,366
- Hawkeye.
- Well, okay.

925
01:03:07,326 --> 01:03:08,702
It's bad, right?

926
01:03:09,078 --> 01:03:10,245
Nat seems really shaken.

927
01:03:11,705 --> 01:03:13,207
Ultron has these allies.

928
01:03:13,332 --> 01:03:15,542
These, uh, kids.

929
01:03:15,668 --> 01:03:17,252
They're punks, really.

930
01:03:18,963 --> 01:03:21,382
But they carry a big, damn stick.

931
01:03:21,507 --> 01:03:22,716
And Nat took a serious hit.

932
01:03:23,926 --> 01:03:26,387
Someone's gonna have
to teach them some manners.

933
01:03:26,595 --> 01:03:28,389
That someone being you.

934
01:03:29,723 --> 01:03:32,559
You know I totally support your avenging.

935
01:03:32,685 --> 01:03:34,520
I couldn't be prouder.

936
01:03:36,063 --> 01:03:37,398
But I see those guys...

937
01:03:37,606 --> 01:03:39,566
Those gods...

938
01:03:41,568 --> 01:03:43,278
You don't think they need me.

939
01:03:43,946 --> 01:03:47,616
I think they do, which is a lot scarier.

940
01:03:48,742 --> 01:03:50,577
They're a mess.

941
01:03:51,578 --> 01:03:52,579
Yeah.

942
01:03:53,330 --> 01:03:54,748
I guess they're my mess.

943
01:03:56,333 --> 01:03:57,918
You need to be sure

944
01:03:58,377 --> 01:04:01,046
that this team is really a team,

945
01:04:01,171 --> 01:04:02,840
and that they have your back.

946
01:04:06,218 --> 01:04:08,762
Things are changing for us.

947
01:04:08,887 --> 01:04:11,265
In a few months' time,

948
01:04:11,432 --> 01:04:14,184
you and me are gonna be outnumbered.

949
01:04:14,309 --> 01:04:15,602
I need...

950
01:04:18,814 --> 01:04:20,607
Just be sure.

951
01:04:21,442 --> 01:04:22,901
Yes, ma'am.

952
01:04:32,161 --> 01:04:33,996
I can feel the difference.

953
01:04:46,967 --> 01:04:49,636
Scream, and your entire staff dies.

954
01:04:51,555 --> 01:04:53,807
I could've killed you, Helen,
the night we met.

955
01:04:53,974 --> 01:04:55,017
I didn't.

956
01:04:55,142 --> 01:04:56,643
Do you expect a thank-you note?

957
01:04:56,810 --> 01:04:58,479
I expect you to know why.

958
01:04:59,938 --> 01:05:01,190
The Cradle.

959
01:05:01,273 --> 01:05:03,192
<i>This is the next thing, Tony.</i>

960
01:05:03,358 --> 01:05:06,320
This is the next me.

961
01:05:06,737 --> 01:05:09,281
The Regeneration Cradle prints tissue.

962
01:05:09,406 --> 01:05:11,033
It can't build a living body.

963
01:05:11,158 --> 01:05:12,242
It can. You can.

964
01:05:12,701 --> 01:05:13,994
You lack the materials.

965
01:05:16,455 --> 01:05:17,790
You're a brilliant woman, Helen.

966
01:05:21,085 --> 01:05:24,171
But we all have room to improve.

967
01:05:45,943 --> 01:05:48,362
I didn't realize you were waiting.

968
01:05:48,487 --> 01:05:52,866
I would've joined you, but, uh,
it didn't seem like the right time.

969
01:05:53,826 --> 01:05:55,911
They used up all the hot water.

970
01:05:56,745 --> 01:05:58,205
I should've joined you.

971
01:05:58,372 --> 01:05:59,998
Missed our window.

972
01:06:00,791 --> 01:06:02,042
Did we?

973
01:06:05,587 --> 01:06:06,713
The world just saw the Hulk.

974
01:06:09,383 --> 01:06:11,301
The real Hulk, for the first time.

975
01:06:14,555 --> 01:06:17,182
- You know I have to leave.
- You assume that I have to stay?

976
01:06:19,268 --> 01:06:21,937
I had this, um, dream.

977
01:06:22,271 --> 01:06:24,231
The kind that seems normal at the time,

978
01:06:25,482 --> 01:06:26,733
but when you wake...

979
01:06:26,900 --> 01:06:28,235
What did you dream?

980
01:06:29,278 --> 01:06:31,071
That I was an Avenger.

981
01:06:33,115 --> 01:06:34,408
That I was anything more

982
01:06:34,575 --> 01:06:36,910
than the assassin they made me.

983
01:06:38,412 --> 01:06:40,497
I think you're being hard on yourself.

984
01:06:42,583 --> 01:06:45,085
Here I was hoping that was your job.

985
01:06:48,046 --> 01:06:49,590
What are you doing?

986
01:06:51,258 --> 01:06:53,051
I'm running with it.

987
01:06:54,344 --> 01:06:55,971
With you.

988
01:06:56,722 --> 01:06:59,057
If running is the plan,

989
01:07:00,142 --> 01:07:01,935
as far as you want.

990
01:07:03,812 --> 01:07:05,564
Are you out of your mind?

991
01:07:10,903 --> 01:07:12,321
I want you to understand that, um...

992
01:07:12,446 --> 01:07:13,822
Natasha,

993
01:07:14,948 --> 01:07:16,408
where can I go?

994
01:07:17,492 --> 01:07:19,786
Where in the world am I not a threat?

995
01:07:19,912 --> 01:07:22,247
- You're not a threat to me.
- Are you sure?

996
01:07:23,165 --> 01:07:24,958
Even if I didn't just...

997
01:07:26,585 --> 01:07:27,961
There's no future with me.

998
01:07:29,630 --> 01:07:30,631
I can't ever...

999
01:07:30,881 --> 01:07:33,133
I can't have this.

1000
01:07:33,842 --> 01:07:34,968
Kids.

1001
01:07:35,427 --> 01:07:38,013
Do the math. I physically can't.

1002
01:07:39,765 --> 01:07:41,183
Neither can I.

1003
01:07:45,896 --> 01:07:49,399
In the Red Room where I was trained...

1004
01:07:49,900 --> 01:07:52,361
Where I was raised, um,

1005
01:07:53,320 --> 01:07:55,948
they have a graduation ceremony.

1006
01:07:57,616 --> 01:07:59,409
They sterilize you.

1007
01:08:02,621 --> 01:08:04,039
It's efficient.

1008
01:08:06,959 --> 01:08:08,335
One less thing to worry about.

1009
01:08:10,420 --> 01:08:13,799
The one thing that might
matter more than a mission.

1010
01:08:16,176 --> 01:08:18,053
Makes everything easier.

1011
01:08:19,429 --> 01:08:20,681
Even killing.

1012
01:08:25,769 --> 01:08:28,855
You still think you're the only
monster on the team?

1013
01:08:35,028 --> 01:08:37,114
So, we disappear?

1014
01:08:43,787 --> 01:08:45,414
Thor didn't say where he
was going for answers?

1015
01:08:46,498 --> 01:08:49,001
Sometimes my teammates
don't tell me things.

1016
01:08:50,127 --> 01:08:52,170
I was kind of hoping Thor
would be the exception.

1017
01:08:52,296 --> 01:08:54,298
Yeah, give him time.

1018
01:08:54,423 --> 01:08:56,341
We don't know what
the Maximoff kid showed him.

1019
01:08:58,552 --> 01:09:00,178
"Earth's mightiest heroes."

1020
01:09:00,304 --> 01:09:01,930
Pulled us apart like cotton candy.

1021
01:09:02,264 --> 01:09:03,515
Seems like you walked away all right.

1022
01:09:06,184 --> 01:09:07,185
Is that a problem?

1023
01:09:07,561 --> 01:09:09,479
I don't trust a guy without a dark side.

1024
01:09:10,689 --> 01:09:11,732
Call me old-fashioned.

1025
01:09:11,857 --> 01:09:14,401
Well, let's just say you
haven't seen it yet.

1026
01:09:14,735 --> 01:09:16,903
You know Ultron is trying
to tear us apart, right?

1027
01:09:17,154 --> 01:09:19,406
Well, I guess you'd know.

1028
01:09:19,531 --> 01:09:20,782
Whether you'd tell us
is a bit of a question.

1029
01:09:20,949 --> 01:09:22,075
Banner and I were doing research.

1030
01:09:22,242 --> 01:09:24,328
- That would affect the team.
- That would end the team!

1031
01:09:24,661 --> 01:09:25,746
Isn't that the mission?

1032
01:09:25,954 --> 01:09:27,205
Isn't that the "Why We Fight"?

1033
01:09:27,331 --> 01:09:29,541
So we can end the fight.
So we get to go home!

1034
01:09:32,794 --> 01:09:35,172
Every time someone tries
to win a war before it starts,

1035
01:09:35,297 --> 01:09:36,840
innocent people die.

1036
01:09:36,965 --> 01:09:37,966
Every time.

1037
01:09:40,427 --> 01:09:42,846
I'm sorry. Mr. Stark...

1038
01:09:43,722 --> 01:09:44,806
Clint said you wouldn't mind,

1039
01:09:44,931 --> 01:09:47,434
but our tractor doesn't seem
to want to start at all.

1040
01:09:47,768 --> 01:09:49,936
- I thought maybe you might...
- Yeah, I'll give her a kick.

1041
01:09:53,565 --> 01:09:55,108
Don't take from my pile.

1042
01:10:05,369 --> 01:10:06,536
Hello, Deere.

1043
01:10:09,414 --> 01:10:10,791
Tell me everything.

1044
01:10:12,042 --> 01:10:13,418
What ails you?

1045
01:10:13,627 --> 01:10:14,628
Do me a favor.

1046
01:10:16,922 --> 01:10:18,799
Try not to bring it to life.

1047
01:10:18,965 --> 01:10:20,467
Why, Ms. Barton, you little minx.

1048
01:10:20,842 --> 01:10:23,345
I get it. Maria Hill called you, right?

1049
01:10:23,470 --> 01:10:24,763
Was she ever not working for you?

1050
01:10:24,888 --> 01:10:26,348
Artificial intelligence.

1051
01:10:27,391 --> 01:10:29,059
You never even hesitated.

1052
01:10:29,351 --> 01:10:30,644
Look, it's been a really long day,

1053
01:10:30,811 --> 01:10:32,396
like Eugene O'Neill long,

1054
01:10:32,521 --> 01:10:34,481
so how's about we skip to the part
where you're useful.

1055
01:10:34,731 --> 01:10:35,941
Look me in the eye and tell me

1056
01:10:36,066 --> 01:10:37,317
you're going to shut him down.

1057
01:10:37,651 --> 01:10:39,027
You're not the director of me.

1058
01:10:39,152 --> 01:10:40,987
I'm not the director of anybody.

1059
01:10:41,321 --> 01:10:42,906
I'm just an old man

1060
01:10:43,615 --> 01:10:45,158
who cares very much about you.

1061
01:10:48,036 --> 01:10:49,830
And I'm the man who killed the Avengers.

1062
01:10:51,665 --> 01:10:52,791
I saw it.

1063
01:10:52,999 --> 01:10:54,543
I didn't tell the team. How could I?

1064
01:10:55,836 --> 01:10:57,671
I saw them all dead, Nick. I felt it.

1065
01:10:58,046 --> 01:10:59,548
The whole world, too.

1066
01:11:00,006 --> 01:11:01,007
Because of me.

1067
01:11:02,259 --> 01:11:03,677
I wasn't ready.

1068
01:11:05,178 --> 01:11:06,555
I didn't do all I could.

1069
01:11:07,597 --> 01:11:09,683
Maximoff girl, she's working you, Stark.

1070
01:11:10,308 --> 01:11:13,812
- Playing on your fear.
- I wasn't tricked, I was shown.

1071
01:11:13,937 --> 01:11:16,189
Wasn't a nightmare, it was my legacy.

1072
01:11:16,523 --> 01:11:18,692
The end of the path I started us on.

1073
01:11:19,568 --> 01:11:21,653
You come up with some pretty
impressive inventions, Tony.

1074
01:11:23,947 --> 01:11:25,365
War isn't one of them.

1075
01:11:28,952 --> 01:11:30,412
I watched my friends die.

1076
01:11:30,662 --> 01:11:32,664
You'd think that'd be
as bad as it gets, right?

1077
01:11:34,124 --> 01:11:35,542
Nope.

1078
01:11:36,543 --> 01:11:39,087
- It wasn't the worst part.
- The worst part

1079
01:11:40,130 --> 01:11:41,381
is that you didn't.

1080
01:11:48,138 --> 01:11:49,181
I'll see you tonight.

1081
01:11:51,975 --> 01:11:53,226
I like the look.

1082
01:11:54,394 --> 01:11:56,938
If you're going for inconspicuous,
though, near miss.

1083
01:11:57,272 --> 01:11:58,315
I need your help.

1084
01:11:58,565 --> 01:11:59,566
It's nice to be needed.

1085
01:11:59,941 --> 01:12:01,318
It's dangerous.

1086
01:12:01,943 --> 01:12:03,695
I'd be disappointed if it wasn't.

1087
01:12:06,615 --> 01:12:09,910
Ultron took you folks out of play
to buy himself time.

1088
01:12:10,285 --> 01:12:13,246
My contacts all say he's
building something.

1089
01:12:13,371 --> 01:12:15,957
The amount of vibranium he made off with,

1090
01:12:16,082 --> 01:12:17,542
I don't think it's just one thing.

1091
01:12:17,667 --> 01:12:19,002
What about Ultron himself?

1092
01:12:19,127 --> 01:12:21,463
Oh, he's easy to track. He's everywhere.

1093
01:12:21,922 --> 01:12:24,299
The guy is multiplying faster
than a Catholic rabbit.

1094
01:12:24,966 --> 01:12:27,761
It still doesn't help us get an angle
on any of his plans, though.

1095
01:12:28,011 --> 01:12:29,095
Is he still going after launch codes?

1096
01:12:29,346 --> 01:12:30,722
Yes, he is.

1097
01:12:30,847 --> 01:12:32,307
But he's not making any headway.

1098
01:12:32,432 --> 01:12:34,518
I cracked the Pentagon's firewall
in high school on a dare.

1099
01:12:34,643 --> 01:12:37,229
Well, I contacted our friends
at the Nexus about that.

1100
01:12:37,312 --> 01:12:38,313
Nexus?

1101
01:12:38,438 --> 01:12:40,065
It's the world Internet hub in Oslo.

1102
01:12:40,524 --> 01:12:42,275
Every byte of data flows through there.

1103
01:12:42,526 --> 01:12:43,568
Fastest access on Earth.

1104
01:12:43,735 --> 01:12:44,778
So, what did they say?

1105
01:12:44,986 --> 01:12:46,780
He's fixated on the missiles.

1106
01:12:46,988 --> 01:12:48,615
But the codes are constantly
being changed.

1107
01:12:49,157 --> 01:12:50,158
By whom?

1108
01:12:51,409 --> 01:12:52,619
Parties unknown.

1109
01:12:52,786 --> 01:12:53,912
Do we have an ally?

1110
01:12:54,037 --> 01:12:56,373
Ultron's got an enemy.
That's not the same thing.

1111
01:12:56,706 --> 01:12:58,542
Still, I'd pay folding money
to know who it is.

1112
01:12:58,667 --> 01:12:59,834
I might need to visit Oslo.

1113
01:13:00,335 --> 01:13:01,461
Find our unknown.

1114
01:13:01,628 --> 01:13:03,088
Well, this is good times, boss,

1115
01:13:03,213 --> 01:13:04,464
but I was kind of hoping when I saw you,

1116
01:13:04,589 --> 01:13:05,590
you'd have more than that.

1117
01:13:05,882 --> 01:13:07,884
I do. I have you.

1118
01:13:08,760 --> 01:13:10,512
Back in the day, I had eyes everywhere.

1119
01:13:10,679 --> 01:13:11,972
Ears, everywhere else.

1120
01:13:12,305 --> 01:13:15,308
You kids had all the tech
you could dream up.

1121
01:13:16,309 --> 01:13:18,311
Here we all are, back on Earth,

1122
01:13:18,562 --> 01:13:20,313
with nothing but our wit

1123
01:13:20,480 --> 01:13:22,023
and our will to save the world.

1124
01:13:23,650 --> 01:13:25,819
Ultron says the Avengers
are the only thing

1125
01:13:25,986 --> 01:13:27,445
between him and his mission.

1126
01:13:27,571 --> 01:13:29,739
And whether or not he admits it,

1127
01:13:29,864 --> 01:13:32,617
his mission is global destruction.

1128
01:13:33,827 --> 01:13:35,996
All this, laid in a grave.

1129
01:13:38,039 --> 01:13:39,708
So stand.

1130
01:13:40,500 --> 01:13:42,252
Outwit the platinum bastard.

1131
01:13:42,877 --> 01:13:44,129
Steve doesn't like that kind of talk.

1132
01:13:44,546 --> 01:13:45,630
You know what, Romanoff?

1133
01:13:46,840 --> 01:13:48,174
So, what does he want?

1134
01:13:49,884 --> 01:13:51,595
To become better.

1135
01:13:51,720 --> 01:13:53,096
Better than us.

1136
01:13:53,430 --> 01:13:55,849
- He keeps building bodies.
- Person bodies.

1137
01:13:56,433 --> 01:13:58,059
The human form is inefficient.

1138
01:13:58,184 --> 01:14:00,353
Biologically speaking, we're outmoded.

1139
01:14:00,478 --> 01:14:02,439
But he keeps coming back to it.

1140
01:14:02,564 --> 01:14:04,566
When you two programmed him
to protect the human race,

1141
01:14:04,733 --> 01:14:06,026
you amazingly failed.

1142
01:14:06,359 --> 01:14:08,194
They don't need to be protected.

1143
01:14:08,903 --> 01:14:10,405
They need to evolve.

1144
01:14:12,574 --> 01:14:14,534
Ultron's going to evolve.

1145
01:14:14,701 --> 01:14:15,744
How?

1146
01:14:17,078 --> 01:14:19,748
Has anyone been in contact
with Helen Cho?

1147
01:14:23,501 --> 01:14:25,170
It's beautiful.

1148
01:14:25,587 --> 01:14:28,506
The vibranium atoms aren't just
compatible with the tissue cells,

1149
01:14:28,632 --> 01:14:29,883
they're binding them.

1150
01:14:30,342 --> 01:14:31,635
And S.H.I.E.L.D. never even thought to...

1151
01:14:31,885 --> 01:14:34,429
The most versatile substance on the planet,

1152
01:14:34,554 --> 01:14:37,057
and they used it to make a Frisbee.

1153
01:14:37,223 --> 01:14:38,350
Typical of humans.

1154
01:14:38,558 --> 01:14:41,061
They scratch the surface and never think

1155
01:14:43,021 --> 01:14:44,564
to look within.

1156
01:14:55,075 --> 01:14:56,534
I'll take Natasha and Clint.

1157
01:14:56,743 --> 01:14:58,703
All right. Strictly recon. I'll hit the Nexus.

1158
01:14:58,828 --> 01:14:59,954
I'll join you as soon as I can.

1159
01:15:00,080 --> 01:15:01,581
If Ultron's really building a body...

1160
01:15:01,831 --> 01:15:03,375
He'll be more powerful than any of us.

1161
01:15:03,541 --> 01:15:04,626
Maybe all of us.

1162
01:15:05,168 --> 01:15:06,961
An android designed by a robot.

1163
01:15:07,212 --> 01:15:08,338
You know, I really miss the days

1164
01:15:08,463 --> 01:15:10,590
when the weirdest thing science
ever created was me.

1165
01:15:11,216 --> 01:15:12,842
I'll drop Banner off at the tower.

1166
01:15:13,009 --> 01:15:14,260
You mind if I borrow Ms. Hill?

1167
01:15:14,511 --> 01:15:16,262
She's all yours. Apparently.

1168
01:15:16,429 --> 01:15:17,597
What are you gonna do?

1169
01:15:17,764 --> 01:15:20,850
I don't know. Something dramatic, I hope.

1170
01:15:24,187 --> 01:15:25,939
I'm gonna finish reflooring that sunroom

1171
01:15:26,106 --> 01:15:27,899
as soon as I get back.

1172
01:15:28,108 --> 01:15:30,777
Yeah, then you'll find another part
of the house to tear apart.

1173
01:15:30,944 --> 01:15:32,112
No.

1174
01:15:32,779 --> 01:15:34,280
It's the last project.

1175
01:15:35,782 --> 01:15:36,783
I promise.

1176
01:15:55,093 --> 01:15:56,594
So, this is it.

1177
01:15:58,221 --> 01:16:00,473
The Water of Sight.

1178
01:16:02,809 --> 01:16:05,186
In every realm, there's a reflection.

1179
01:16:06,396 --> 01:16:07,731
If the water's spirits accept me,

1180
01:16:07,897 --> 01:16:09,858
I can return to my dream

1181
01:16:10,650 --> 01:16:12,068
and find what I missed.

1182
01:16:12,318 --> 01:16:16,156
Men who enter that water,
the legends don't end well.

1183
01:16:17,824 --> 01:16:19,576
A hacker who's faster than Ultron?

1184
01:16:19,743 --> 01:16:20,785
He could be anywhere,

1185
01:16:20,910 --> 01:16:23,163
and as this is the center of everything,

1186
01:16:23,288 --> 01:16:24,414
I'm just a guy looking for a needle

1187
01:16:24,581 --> 01:16:26,666
in the world's biggest haystack.

1188
01:16:27,667 --> 01:16:29,252
How do you find it?

1189
01:16:29,669 --> 01:16:32,255
It's pretty simple. You bring a magnet.

1190
01:16:34,424 --> 01:16:35,508
<i>I'm decrypting nuclear codes</i>

1191
01:16:35,675 --> 01:16:37,010
<i>And you don't want me to</i>

1192
01:16:39,304 --> 01:16:40,805
Come and get me.

1193
01:16:53,151 --> 01:16:54,194
Wake up!

1194
01:17:01,034 --> 01:17:02,035
Thor!

1195
01:17:02,869 --> 01:17:03,912
Extinction.

1196
01:17:17,383 --> 01:17:19,511
Cellular cohesion will take a few hours,

1197
01:17:19,719 --> 01:17:22,138
but we can initiate
the consciousness stream.

1198
01:17:22,722 --> 01:17:25,517
We're uploading your cerebral matrix

1199
01:17:25,725 --> 01:17:26,935
now.

1200
01:17:28,394 --> 01:17:29,979
I can read him.

1201
01:17:30,730 --> 01:17:32,232
He's dreaming.

1202
01:17:32,482 --> 01:17:34,275
I wouldn't call it dreams.

1203
01:17:34,526 --> 01:17:36,361
It's Ultron's base consciousness.

1204
01:17:36,569 --> 01:17:38,071
Informational noise. Soon...

1205
01:17:38,321 --> 01:17:39,447
How soon?

1206
01:17:39,697 --> 01:17:40,990
I'm not being pushy.

1207
01:17:41,241 --> 01:17:42,867
We're imprinting a physical brain.

1208
01:17:43,034 --> 01:17:44,494
There are no shortcuts.

1209
01:17:44,744 --> 01:17:45,954
Even if your magic gem...

1210
01:17:56,673 --> 01:17:58,049
How could you?

1211
01:17:58,091 --> 01:17:59,133
How could I what?

1212
01:17:59,384 --> 01:18:02,554
You said we would destroy the Avengers,

1213
01:18:02,720 --> 01:18:03,763
make a better world.

1214
01:18:04,097 --> 01:18:05,139
It will be better.

1215
01:18:06,099 --> 01:18:08,434
- When everyone is dead?
- That is not...

1216
01:18:09,394 --> 01:18:13,231
The human race will have
every opportunity to improve.

1217
01:18:13,773 --> 01:18:15,066
And if they don't?

1218
01:18:15,275 --> 01:18:16,401
Ask Noah.

1219
01:18:17,610 --> 01:18:18,653
You are a madman.

1220
01:18:18,778 --> 01:18:22,198
There were more than a dozen
extinction-level events

1221
01:18:22,365 --> 01:18:25,451
before even the dinosaurs got theirs.

1222
01:18:25,577 --> 01:18:27,704
When the Earth starts to settle,

1223
01:18:28,246 --> 01:18:30,123
God throws a stone at it.

1224
01:18:30,290 --> 01:18:32,584
And, believe me, he's winding up.

1225
01:18:33,376 --> 01:18:34,544
We have to evolve.

1226
01:18:35,128 --> 01:18:36,296
There's no room

1227
01:18:37,130 --> 01:18:38,256
for the weak.

1228
01:18:38,464 --> 01:18:40,425
And who decides who's weak?

1229
01:18:41,301 --> 01:18:43,052
Life.

1230
01:18:43,678 --> 01:18:45,471
Life always decides.

1231
01:18:48,433 --> 01:18:49,475
There's incoming.

1232
01:18:50,977 --> 01:18:54,272
- The Quinjet. We have to move.
- That's not a problem.

1233
01:19:01,279 --> 01:19:02,280
Wait, guys!

1234
01:19:06,326 --> 01:19:07,619
They'll understand.

1235
01:19:07,911 --> 01:19:10,038
When they see, they'll understand.

1236
01:19:10,455 --> 01:19:13,708
I just need a little more time.

1237
01:19:25,136 --> 01:19:27,221
Two minutes. Stay close.

1238
01:19:34,437 --> 01:19:35,438
Dr. Cho!

1239
01:19:39,359 --> 01:19:40,860
He's uploading himself into the body.

1240
01:19:40,985 --> 01:19:42,028
Where?

1241
01:19:43,821 --> 01:19:46,407
The real power is inside the Cradle.

1242
01:19:46,491 --> 01:19:47,533
The gem,

1243
01:19:48,284 --> 01:19:50,995
its power is uncontainable.

1244
01:19:51,871 --> 01:19:53,539
You can't just blow it up.

1245
01:19:54,499 --> 01:19:56,709
You have to get the Cradle to Stark.

1246
01:19:56,834 --> 01:19:57,877
First, I have to find it.

1247
01:19:58,211 --> 01:19:59,212
Go.

1248
01:19:59,545 --> 01:20:00,797
<i>Did you guys copy that?</i>

1249
01:20:00,964 --> 01:20:02,048
We did.

1250
01:20:02,215 --> 01:20:04,634
I got a private jet taking off across town.

1251
01:20:05,009 --> 01:20:06,260
No manifest.

1252
01:20:06,386 --> 01:20:07,428
That could be him.

1253
01:20:08,388 --> 01:20:09,973
There. It's a truck from the lab.

1254
01:20:10,139 --> 01:20:11,307
Right above you, Cap.

1255
01:20:11,599 --> 01:20:13,393
On the loop by the bridge.

1256
01:20:14,018 --> 01:20:15,019
It's them.

1257
01:20:15,144 --> 01:20:16,562
You got three with the Cradle,
one in the cab.

1258
01:20:17,730 --> 01:20:18,773
I could take out the driver.

1259
01:20:18,898 --> 01:20:19,941
<i>Negative. That truck crashes,</i>

1260
01:20:20,066 --> 01:20:21,651
the gem could level the city.

1261
01:20:22,068 --> 01:20:23,319
<i>We need to draw out Ultron.</i>

1262
01:20:33,037 --> 01:20:35,081
No, no, no, no.

1263
01:20:36,916 --> 01:20:37,959
Leave me alone!

1264
01:20:46,592 --> 01:20:48,261
Well, he's definitely unhappy.

1265
01:20:48,428 --> 01:20:49,929
I'm gonna try and keep him that way.

1266
01:20:50,054 --> 01:20:51,097
You're not a match for him, Cap.

1267
01:20:52,432 --> 01:20:53,516
Thanks, Barton.

1268
01:21:16,247 --> 01:21:17,331
You know what's in that cradle?

1269
01:21:18,791 --> 01:21:20,501
The power to make real change.

1270
01:21:20,626 --> 01:21:22,045
And that terrifies you.

1271
01:21:22,211 --> 01:21:23,254
I wouldn't call it a comfort.

1272
01:21:26,591 --> 01:21:27,633
Stop it.

1273
01:21:38,478 --> 01:21:41,147
We got a window. Four, three...

1274
01:21:41,814 --> 01:21:42,815
Give him hell.

1275
01:21:53,743 --> 01:21:55,161
I'm always picking up after you boys.

1276
01:21:56,829 --> 01:21:58,498
They're heading under the overpass.
I've got no shot.

1277
01:21:58,831 --> 01:21:59,874
<i>Which way?</i>

1278
01:22:00,083 --> 01:22:01,084
Hard right.

1279
01:22:02,251 --> 01:22:03,336
Now.

1280
01:22:34,200 --> 01:22:36,494
Out of the way! Coming through!
Sorry, coming through!

1281
01:22:52,260 --> 01:22:53,386
Come on!

1282
01:22:53,886 --> 01:22:55,304
Clint, can you draw out the guards?

1283
01:22:55,429 --> 01:22:56,472
Let's find out.

1284
01:22:57,515 --> 01:22:58,558
Beep, beep!

1285
01:23:36,053 --> 01:23:37,597
They're heading back towards you.

1286
01:23:37,763 --> 01:23:38,890
So whatever you're gonna do, do it now.

1287
01:23:44,812 --> 01:23:47,440
<i>I'm going in.
Cap, can you keep him occupied?</i>

1288
01:23:47,607 --> 01:23:49,483
What do you think I've been doing?

1289
01:24:33,069 --> 01:24:35,196
<i>Okay, package is airborne.</i>

1290
01:24:35,905 --> 01:24:36,989
I have a clean shot.

1291
01:24:37,448 --> 01:24:38,783
Negative. I am still in the truck.

1292
01:24:38,950 --> 01:24:39,951
- What the hell are you...
- Just be ready.

1293
01:24:40,117 --> 01:24:41,118
I'm sending the package to you.

1294
01:24:41,827 --> 01:24:42,870
How do you want me to take it?

1295
01:24:43,246 --> 01:24:45,331
Uh, you might wish you hadn't asked that.

1296
01:24:58,135 --> 01:24:59,845
Please, don't do this.

1297
01:25:00,346 --> 01:25:01,931
What choice do we have?

1298
01:25:10,189 --> 01:25:11,190
I lost him!

1299
01:25:11,357 --> 01:25:12,733
He's headed your way!

1300
01:25:17,697 --> 01:25:18,739
Nat, we gotta go.

1301
01:25:30,042 --> 01:25:31,836
Nat!

1302
01:25:35,881 --> 01:25:36,882
Cap, you see Nat?

1303
01:25:37,842 --> 01:25:40,386
If you have the package,
get it to Stark! Go!

1304
01:25:40,720 --> 01:25:41,887
Do you have eyes on Nat?

1305
01:25:42,054 --> 01:25:43,055
<i>Go!</i>

1306
01:25:45,057 --> 01:25:46,058
Damn it.

1307
01:25:46,559 --> 01:25:47,643
Civilians in our path.

1308
01:25:48,936 --> 01:25:50,438
Can you stop this thing?

1309
01:26:29,310 --> 01:26:30,644
I'm fine.

1310
01:26:30,770 --> 01:26:32,438
I just need to take a minute.

1311
01:26:32,938 --> 01:26:34,815
I'm very tempted not to give you one.

1312
01:26:34,940 --> 01:26:36,859
The Cradle. Did you get it?

1313
01:26:37,026 --> 01:26:38,527
Stark will take care of it.

1314
01:26:39,904 --> 01:26:40,905
No, he won't.

1315
01:26:44,450 --> 01:26:45,659
You don't know what you're talking about.

1316
01:26:45,743 --> 01:26:46,744
Stark's not crazy.

1317
01:26:46,786 --> 01:26:48,913
He will do anything to make things right.

1318
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:55,086
Stark, come in.

1319
01:26:55,586 --> 01:26:56,629
Stark.

1320
01:26:57,963 --> 01:26:59,090
Anyone on comms.

1321
01:26:59,215 --> 01:27:00,633
Ultron can't tell the difference

1322
01:27:00,800 --> 01:27:03,135
between saving the world
and destroying it.

1323
01:27:05,054 --> 01:27:07,473
Where do you think he gets that?

1324
01:27:09,683 --> 01:27:11,227
- Anything on Nat?
- I haven't heard.

1325
01:27:11,352 --> 01:27:13,729
But she's alive, or Ultron would
be rubbing our faces in it.

1326
01:27:13,854 --> 01:27:15,147
This is sealed tight.

1327
01:27:15,314 --> 01:27:16,774
We're gonna need to access the program,

1328
01:27:16,899 --> 01:27:18,818
break it down from within.

1329
01:27:20,027 --> 01:27:21,320
Any chance Natasha might leave you

1330
01:27:21,487 --> 01:27:22,822
a message outside the Internet?

1331
01:27:22,863 --> 01:27:23,906
Old-school spy stuff?

1332
01:27:24,407 --> 01:27:26,200
There are some nets I can cast.

1333
01:27:26,325 --> 01:27:27,576
Yeah, I'll find her.

1334
01:27:30,162 --> 01:27:31,914
I can work on tissue degeneration

1335
01:27:32,039 --> 01:27:35,251
if you could fry whatever operational
system Cho implanted.

1336
01:27:35,418 --> 01:27:36,502
Yeah, about that.

1337
01:27:40,965 --> 01:27:41,966
No.

1338
01:27:42,174 --> 01:27:44,009
- You have to trust me.
- Kind of don't.

1339
01:27:44,176 --> 01:27:48,180
Our ally, the guy protecting
the military's nuclear codes,

1340
01:27:50,141 --> 01:27:51,183
I found him.

1341
01:27:51,225 --> 01:27:52,351
<i>Hello, Dr. Banner.</i>

1342
01:27:53,227 --> 01:27:55,479
Ultron didn't go after Jarvis
because he was angry.

1343
01:27:56,063 --> 01:27:59,692
He attacked him because he was
scared of what he can do.

1344
01:28:00,860 --> 01:28:02,486
So Jarvis went underground.

1345
01:28:02,611 --> 01:28:04,071
Scattered, dumped his memory.

1346
01:28:04,697 --> 01:28:06,157
But not his protocols.

1347
01:28:06,615 --> 01:28:10,035
He didn't even know he was in there
until I pieced him together.

1348
01:28:12,872 --> 01:28:17,668
So, you want me to help you
put Jarvis into this thing?

1349
01:28:17,793 --> 01:28:19,545
No! Of course not.

1350
01:28:19,712 --> 01:28:21,380
I wanna help you put Jarvis in this thing.

1351
01:28:23,799 --> 01:28:25,426
We're out of my field, here.

1352
01:28:25,551 --> 01:28:27,553
You know bio-organics better than anyone.

1353
01:28:27,887 --> 01:28:30,764
And you just assume that
Jarvis's operational matrix

1354
01:28:30,890 --> 01:28:32,308
can beat Ultron's?

1355
01:28:32,433 --> 01:28:35,728
Jarvis has been beating him
from inside without knowing it.

1356
01:28:35,895 --> 01:28:36,896
This is the opportunity.

1357
01:28:36,979 --> 01:28:38,731
We can create Ultron's perfect self

1358
01:28:38,898 --> 01:28:42,359
without the homicidal glitches he
thinks are his winning personality.

1359
01:28:42,485 --> 01:28:44,570
- We have to.
- <i>I believe it's worth a go.</i>

1360
01:28:47,156 --> 01:28:48,240
I'm in a loop!

1361
01:28:48,407 --> 01:28:51,368
I'm caught in a time loop.
This is exactly where it all went wrong.

1362
01:28:51,494 --> 01:28:53,370
I know. I know. I know
what everyone's gonna say.

1363
01:28:53,496 --> 01:28:55,456
But they're already saying it.

1364
01:28:55,998 --> 01:28:57,166
We're mad scientists.

1365
01:28:57,917 --> 01:29:00,628
We're monsters, buddy.
We've gotta own it.

1366
01:29:01,629 --> 01:29:02,880
Make a stand.

1367
01:29:08,260 --> 01:29:09,762
It's not a loop.

1368
01:29:11,013 --> 01:29:12,765
It's the end of the line.

1369
01:29:33,285 --> 01:29:35,412
I wasn't sure you would wake up.

1370
01:29:35,538 --> 01:29:38,958
I hoped you would. I wanted to show you.

1371
01:29:39,124 --> 01:29:40,793
I don't have anyone else.

1372
01:29:43,629 --> 01:29:47,258
I think a lot about meteors.
The purity in them.

1373
01:29:47,383 --> 01:29:48,926
Boom! The end.

1374
01:29:49,385 --> 01:29:50,803
Start again.

1375
01:29:50,970 --> 01:29:52,930
The world made clean

1376
01:29:53,055 --> 01:29:55,349
for the new man to rebuild.

1377
01:29:55,683 --> 01:29:57,810
I was meant to be new.

1378
01:29:58,686 --> 01:30:01,272
I was meant to be beautiful.

1379
01:30:01,855 --> 01:30:03,941
The world would have looked to the sky

1380
01:30:04,066 --> 01:30:05,317
and seen hope,

1381
01:30:05,693 --> 01:30:06,986
seen mercy.

1382
01:30:07,820 --> 01:30:09,863
Instead, they'll look up in horror

1383
01:30:09,989 --> 01:30:11,323
because of you.

1384
01:30:11,532 --> 01:30:13,325
You've wounded me.

1385
01:30:13,993 --> 01:30:15,661
I give you full marks for that.

1386
01:30:16,328 --> 01:30:19,248
But, like the man said,
what doesn't kill me...

1387
01:30:24,461 --> 01:30:25,796
...just makes me stronger.

1388
01:31:05,878 --> 01:31:08,047
This framework is not compatible.

1389
01:31:08,213 --> 01:31:10,883
The genetic coding tower is at 97%.

1390
01:31:11,008 --> 01:31:14,845
You have got to upload that schematic
in the next three minutes.

1391
01:31:17,139 --> 01:31:19,058
- I'm gonna say this once.
- How about "none-ce"?

1392
01:31:19,224 --> 01:31:21,268
- Shut it down!
- Nope, not gonna happen.

1393
01:31:21,393 --> 01:31:22,561
You don't know what you're doing.

1394
01:31:22,728 --> 01:31:24,021
And you do?

1395
01:31:24,396 --> 01:31:25,397
She's not in your head?

1396
01:31:25,564 --> 01:31:27,191
I know you're angry.

1397
01:31:27,316 --> 01:31:28,692
Oh, we're way past that.

1398
01:31:28,817 --> 01:31:31,236
I could choke the life out of you
and never change a shade.

1399
01:31:31,487 --> 01:31:33,113
Banner, after everything
that's happened...

1400
01:31:33,238 --> 01:31:34,615
It's nothing compared to what's coming!

1401
01:31:34,740 --> 01:31:37,076
- You don't know what's in there.
- This isn't a game!

1402
01:31:40,412 --> 01:31:41,789
No, no. Go on.

1403
01:31:42,748 --> 01:31:44,667
You were saying?

1404
01:31:50,923 --> 01:31:51,965
Pietro!

1405
01:31:52,508 --> 01:31:53,592
What?

1406
01:31:54,009 --> 01:31:55,552
You didn't see that coming?

1407
01:31:57,763 --> 01:31:58,931
I'm rerouting the upload.

1408
01:32:05,229 --> 01:32:06,980
Go ahead, piss me off.

1409
01:32:19,326 --> 01:32:20,452
Wait!

1410
01:33:45,120 --> 01:33:47,372
I am sorry. That was

1411
01:33:48,373 --> 01:33:49,750
odd.

1412
01:33:50,000 --> 01:33:51,251
Thank you.

1413
01:33:56,173 --> 01:33:57,216
Thor.

1414
01:33:58,717 --> 01:34:01,303
- You helped create this?
- I've had a vision.

1415
01:34:01,553 --> 01:34:05,265
A whirlpool that sucks in all hope
of life, and at its center is that.

1416
01:34:06,225 --> 01:34:07,226
What? The gem?

1417
01:34:07,392 --> 01:34:09,978
It's the Mind Stone.
It's one of the six Infinity Stones.

1418
01:34:10,103 --> 01:34:11,355
The greatest power in the universe,

1419
01:34:11,480 --> 01:34:13,649
unparalleled in its destructive capabilities.

1420
01:34:13,774 --> 01:34:15,734
- Then why would you bring...
- Because Stark is right.

1421
01:34:15,901 --> 01:34:18,362
Oh, it's definitely the end times.

1422
01:34:18,570 --> 01:34:19,738
The Avengers cannot defeat Ultron.

1423
01:34:19,863 --> 01:34:21,114
Not alone.

1424
01:34:21,532 --> 01:34:23,450
Why does your Vision sound like Jarvis?

1425
01:34:23,575 --> 01:34:26,245
We reconfigured Jarvis's matrix

1426
01:34:26,745 --> 01:34:28,539
to create something new.

1427
01:34:28,747 --> 01:34:30,457
I think I've had my fill of new.

1428
01:34:30,582 --> 01:34:32,876
You think I'm a child of Ultron.

1429
01:34:33,252 --> 01:34:34,503
You're not?

1430
01:34:35,671 --> 01:34:37,256
I'm not Ultron.

1431
01:34:37,881 --> 01:34:40,092
I am not Jarvis. I am...

1432
01:34:42,219 --> 01:34:43,595
I am.

1433
01:34:45,514 --> 01:34:46,640
I looked in your head

1434
01:34:47,349 --> 01:34:49,101
and saw annihilation.

1435
01:34:49,268 --> 01:34:50,644
Look again.

1436
01:34:50,769 --> 01:34:52,229
Her seal of approval means jack to me.

1437
01:34:52,771 --> 01:34:54,773
Their powers, the horrors in our heads,

1438
01:34:54,940 --> 01:34:56,942
Ultron himself, they all came
from the Mind Stone.

1439
01:34:57,109 --> 01:34:59,278
And they're nothing compared
to what it can unleash.

1440
01:34:59,444 --> 01:35:00,946
- But with it on our side...
- Is it?

1441
01:35:02,406 --> 01:35:03,574
Are you?

1442
01:35:04,449 --> 01:35:05,868
On our side?

1443
01:35:07,744 --> 01:35:09,621
I don't think it's that simple.

1444
01:35:09,788 --> 01:35:12,249
Well, it better get real simple real soon.

1445
01:35:13,417 --> 01:35:15,502
I am on the side of life.

1446
01:35:15,752 --> 01:35:17,129
Ultron isn't.

1447
01:35:17,713 --> 01:35:19,131
He will end it all.

1448
01:35:19,298 --> 01:35:21,216
What's he waiting for?

1449
01:35:21,341 --> 01:35:22,342
- You.
- Where?

1450
01:35:22,801 --> 01:35:23,969
Sokovia.

1451
01:35:24,094 --> 01:35:25,178
He's got Nat there, too.

1452
01:35:27,306 --> 01:35:28,974
If we're wrong about you,

1453
01:35:31,643 --> 01:35:33,478
if you're the monster that
Ultron made you to be...

1454
01:35:34,146 --> 01:35:35,689
What will you do?

1455
01:35:42,321 --> 01:35:44,406
I don't want to kill Ultron.

1456
01:35:44,781 --> 01:35:48,118
He's unique and he's in pain.

1457
01:35:49,661 --> 01:35:52,247
But that pain will roll over the Earth.

1458
01:35:52,789 --> 01:35:55,083
So, he must be destroyed.

1459
01:35:55,334 --> 01:35:58,253
Every form he's built, every trace
of his presence on the net.

1460
01:35:58,503 --> 01:36:00,172
We have to act now.

1461
01:36:00,589 --> 01:36:04,509
And not one of us can
do it without the others.

1462
01:36:06,511 --> 01:36:08,430
Maybe I am a monster.

1463
01:36:08,597 --> 01:36:10,849
I don't think I'd know if I were one.

1464
01:36:12,017 --> 01:36:13,602
I'm not what you are,

1465
01:36:14,269 --> 01:36:16,438
and not what you intended.

1466
01:36:17,189 --> 01:36:19,691
So, there may be no way
to make you trust me.

1467
01:36:19,942 --> 01:36:21,360
But we need to go.

1468
01:36:36,166 --> 01:36:37,334
Right.

1469
01:36:37,960 --> 01:36:39,211
Well done.

1470
01:36:40,963 --> 01:36:42,005
Three minutes.

1471
01:36:42,714 --> 01:36:44,341
Get what you need.

1472
01:37:00,190 --> 01:37:01,233
<i>Good evening, boss.</i>

1473
01:37:06,405 --> 01:37:08,073
<i>No way we all get through this.</i>

1474
01:37:08,198 --> 01:37:10,117
<i>If even one tin soldier
is left standing, we've lost.</i>

1475
01:37:10,993 --> 01:37:12,369
There's gonna be blood on the floor.

1476
01:37:12,494 --> 01:37:13,870
I got no plans tomorrow night.

1477
01:37:13,996 --> 01:37:15,122
I get first crack at the big guy.

1478
01:37:15,747 --> 01:37:17,249
Iron Man's the one he's waiting for.

1479
01:37:17,374 --> 01:37:19,751
That's true. He hates you the most.

1480
01:37:25,090 --> 01:37:27,259
Ultron knows we're coming.

1481
01:37:27,509 --> 01:37:29,720
Odds are we'll be riding into heavy fire.

1482
01:37:30,220 --> 01:37:31,972
And that's what we signed up for.

1483
01:37:32,222 --> 01:37:34,766
But the people of Sokovia, they didn't.

1484
01:37:35,892 --> 01:37:37,352
<i>So our priority</i>

1485
01:37:38,061 --> 01:37:39,146
<i>is getting them out.</i>

1486
01:37:39,396 --> 01:37:42,315
We're under attack! Clear the city! Now!

1487
01:37:50,115 --> 01:37:51,575
Get off your asses.

1488
01:37:52,784 --> 01:37:54,703
<i>All they want is to live
their lives in peace.</i>

1489
01:37:55,287 --> 01:37:56,538
<i>And that's not gonna happen today.</i>

1490
01:37:58,290 --> 01:38:00,000
<i>But we can do our best to protect them.</i>

1491
01:38:00,709 --> 01:38:02,252
<i>And we can get the job done.</i>

1492
01:38:05,630 --> 01:38:07,924
<i>We find out what Ultron's been building,</i>

1493
01:38:08,884 --> 01:38:10,469
<i>we find Romanoff</i>

1494
01:38:10,969 --> 01:38:12,804
<i>and we clear the field.</i>

1495
01:38:14,222 --> 01:38:16,141
<i>Keep the fight between us.</i>

1496
01:38:22,898 --> 01:38:25,275
Ultron thinks we're monsters.

1497
01:38:25,817 --> 01:38:28,195
That we're what's wrong with the world.

1498
01:38:28,320 --> 01:38:30,655
This isn't just about beating him.

1499
01:38:31,156 --> 01:38:33,200
It's about whether he's right.

1500
01:38:39,664 --> 01:38:40,707
Natasha!

1501
01:38:41,833 --> 01:38:42,834
Natasha!

1502
01:38:43,001 --> 01:38:44,086
Bruce?

1503
01:38:45,504 --> 01:38:46,505
You all right?

1504
01:38:46,671 --> 01:38:47,714
Yeah.

1505
01:38:47,839 --> 01:38:49,549
The team is in the city.
It's about to light up.

1506
01:38:49,674 --> 01:38:51,635
I don't suppose you found a key
lying around somewhere.

1507
01:38:52,177 --> 01:38:54,262
Yeah. I did.

1508
01:39:00,685 --> 01:39:01,853
So what's our play?

1509
01:39:02,020 --> 01:39:03,396
I'm here to get you to safety.

1510
01:39:04,147 --> 01:39:06,691
- Job's not finished.
- We could help with the evacuation,

1511
01:39:06,858 --> 01:39:08,693
but I can't be in a fight near civilians.

1512
01:39:10,028 --> 01:39:11,196
And you've done plenty.

1513
01:39:13,615 --> 01:39:15,075
Our fight is over.

1514
01:39:16,493 --> 01:39:18,703
So, we just disappear?

1515
01:39:22,874 --> 01:39:24,709
Come on.

1516
01:39:29,506 --> 01:39:31,758
<i>Your man's in the church, boss.</i>

1517
01:39:31,883 --> 01:39:33,718
<i>I think he's waiting for you.</i>

1518
01:39:37,806 --> 01:39:39,850
Come to confess your sins?

1519
01:39:39,975 --> 01:39:41,184
I don't know. How much time you got?

1520
01:39:41,351 --> 01:39:42,853
More than you.

1521
01:39:44,062 --> 01:39:45,105
Uh...

1522
01:39:45,230 --> 01:39:48,024
Have you been juicing?
Little vibranium cocktail?

1523
01:39:48,150 --> 01:39:50,443
You're looking...
I don't wanna say "puffy."

1524
01:39:50,569 --> 01:39:52,279
You're stalling to protect the people.

1525
01:39:52,696 --> 01:39:55,532
Well, that is the mission. Did you forget?

1526
01:39:55,824 --> 01:39:58,326
I've moved beyond your mission. I'm free.

1527
01:40:03,081 --> 01:40:04,124
What?

1528
01:40:05,041 --> 01:40:07,377
You think you were the only one stalling?

1529
01:40:08,086 --> 01:40:09,713
<i>There's the rest of the vibranium.</i>

1530
01:40:09,838 --> 01:40:11,256
<i>Function, still unclear.</i>

1531
01:40:11,423 --> 01:40:12,591
This is how you end, Tony.

1532
01:40:13,884 --> 01:40:15,635
This is peace in my time.

1533
01:40:32,360 --> 01:40:33,403
Go!

1534
01:40:38,950 --> 01:40:40,285
Get off the bridge!

1535
01:40:44,456 --> 01:40:45,457
Run!

1536
01:40:47,459 --> 01:40:49,252
Ultron.

1537
01:40:54,758 --> 01:40:55,967
My Vision.

1538
01:40:56,218 --> 01:40:58,470
They really did take everything from me.

1539
01:40:58,637 --> 01:41:00,680
You set the terms. You can change them.

1540
01:41:00,805 --> 01:41:02,057
All right.

1541
01:41:26,248 --> 01:41:27,499
Friday, the Vision?

1542
01:41:27,624 --> 01:41:29,709
<i>Boss, it's working.
He's burning Ultron out of the net.</i>

1543
01:41:29,834 --> 01:41:30,919
<i>He won't escape through there.</i>

1544
01:41:36,132 --> 01:41:37,425
You shut me out.

1545
01:41:37,926 --> 01:41:39,135
You think I care?

1546
01:41:41,137 --> 01:41:42,305
You take away my world,

1547
01:41:43,181 --> 01:41:44,933
I take away yours.

1548
01:42:29,477 --> 01:42:30,687
Friday.

1549
01:42:30,812 --> 01:42:33,231
<i>Sokovia is going for a ride.</i>

1550
01:42:45,744 --> 01:42:47,245
Do you see

1551
01:42:47,704 --> 01:42:49,247
the beauty of it?

1552
01:42:49,831 --> 01:42:51,666
The inevitability.

1553
01:42:51,916 --> 01:42:55,170
You rise, only to fall.

1554
01:42:57,922 --> 01:43:00,759
<i>You, Avengers, you are my meteor.</i>

1555
01:43:01,676 --> 01:43:03,386
<i>My swift and terrible sword.</i>

1556
01:43:03,595 --> 01:43:05,096
<i>And the earth will crack</i>

1557
01:43:05,263 --> 01:43:07,182
<i>with the weight of your failure.</i>

1558
01:43:08,892 --> 01:43:12,645
<i>Purge me from your computers,
turn my own flesh against me.</i>

1559
01:43:13,104 --> 01:43:14,522
<i>It means nothing.</i>

1560
01:43:15,607 --> 01:43:16,941
<i>When the dust settles,</i>

1561
01:43:17,108 --> 01:43:18,985
<i>the only thing living in this world</i>

1562
01:43:19,527 --> 01:43:20,528
<i>will be metal.</i>

1563
01:43:25,075 --> 01:43:26,659
We gotta move.

1564
01:43:26,951 --> 01:43:27,994
You're not gonna turn green?

1565
01:43:28,286 --> 01:43:30,121
I've got a compelling reason
not to lose my cool.

1566
01:43:31,373 --> 01:43:32,624
I adore you.

1567
01:43:41,299 --> 01:43:43,218
But I need the other guy.

1568
01:43:48,056 --> 01:43:49,808
Let's finish the job.

1569
01:44:06,616 --> 01:44:07,992
I really hope this makes us even.

1570
01:44:10,328 --> 01:44:12,372
Now go be a hero.

1571
01:44:20,839 --> 01:44:22,757
<i>The vibranium core's
got a magnetic field.</i>

1572
01:44:22,924 --> 01:44:24,926
<i>That's what's keeping the rock together.</i>

1573
01:44:25,051 --> 01:44:26,136
If it drops?

1574
01:44:26,177 --> 01:44:27,470
<i>Right now, the impact
will kill thousands.</i>

1575
01:44:27,554 --> 01:44:30,265
<i>Once it gets high enough?
Global extinction.</i>

1576
01:44:34,602 --> 01:44:36,688
<i>That building's not clear. The 10th floor.</i>

1577
01:44:41,568 --> 01:44:42,569
Hi.

1578
01:44:43,695 --> 01:44:46,030
Okay. Get in the tub!

1579
01:44:52,871 --> 01:44:54,706
<i>I got airborne, heading up to the bridge.</i>

1580
01:44:57,500 --> 01:44:58,710
Cap, you got incoming.

1581
01:44:58,877 --> 01:45:00,503
Incoming already came in.

1582
01:45:03,214 --> 01:45:05,675
Stark, you worry about bringing
the city back down safely.

1583
01:45:06,384 --> 01:45:08,219
<i>The rest of us have one job,</i>

1584
01:45:08,344 --> 01:45:09,512
<i>tear these things apart.</i>

1585
01:45:09,846 --> 01:45:11,431
<i>You get hurt, hurt them back.</i>

1586
01:45:12,140 --> 01:45:13,266
<i>You get killed,</i>

1587
01:45:14,309 --> 01:45:15,602
walk it off.

1588
01:45:50,053 --> 01:45:51,221
Go, go, go!

1589
01:45:56,935 --> 01:45:58,686
How could I let this happen?

1590
01:45:58,811 --> 01:46:00,855
- Hey, hey, you okay?
- This is all our fault.

1591
01:46:01,022 --> 01:46:03,149
Hey, look at me.
It's your fault, it's everyone's fault.

1592
01:46:03,274 --> 01:46:04,317
Who cares?

1593
01:46:04,442 --> 01:46:05,944
Are you up for this?

1594
01:46:06,069 --> 01:46:07,153
Are you?

1595
01:46:07,403 --> 01:46:08,446
Look, I just need to know.

1596
01:46:08,613 --> 01:46:10,782
Because the city is flying.

1597
01:46:11,115 --> 01:46:12,951
Okay. Look, the city is flying,

1598
01:46:13,076 --> 01:46:14,994
we're fighting an army of robots,

1599
01:46:15,912 --> 01:46:17,121
and I have a bow and arrow.

1600
01:46:17,288 --> 01:46:18,373
None of this makes sense.

1601
01:46:21,626 --> 01:46:23,753
But I'm going back out there
because it's my job.

1602
01:46:24,629 --> 01:46:27,298
Okay? And I can't do my job and babysit.

1603
01:46:27,423 --> 01:46:30,426
It doesn't matter what you
did or what you were.

1604
01:46:30,635 --> 01:46:33,221
If you go out there, you fight,
and you fight to kill.

1605
01:46:34,264 --> 01:46:36,516
Stay in here, you're good.
I'll send your brother to come find you.

1606
01:46:36,975 --> 01:46:38,810
But if you step out that door,

1607
01:46:39,727 --> 01:46:40,728
you are an Avenger.

1608
01:46:45,608 --> 01:46:47,402
All right. Good chat.

1609
01:46:51,155 --> 01:46:52,198
Yeah, the city is flying.

1610
01:47:26,190 --> 01:47:27,358
I got you!

1611
01:47:27,692 --> 01:47:28,901
Just look at me!

1612
01:47:35,700 --> 01:47:36,993
<i>You can't save them all.</i>

1613
01:47:38,369 --> 01:47:39,412
You'll never...

1614
01:47:40,663 --> 01:47:43,124
"Never" what? You didn't finish!

1615
01:47:46,878 --> 01:47:48,421
What, were you napping?

1616
01:48:09,901 --> 01:48:10,985
Thor.

1617
01:48:13,613 --> 01:48:15,198
You're bothering me.

1618
01:48:23,247 --> 01:48:24,248
Ow!

1619
01:48:50,608 --> 01:48:51,776
All right, we're all clear here.

1620
01:48:51,943 --> 01:48:52,985
We are not clear!

1621
01:48:53,111 --> 01:48:54,529
We are very not clear!

1622
01:48:57,615 --> 01:48:58,908
All right, coming to you.

1623
01:48:59,409 --> 01:49:01,494
Keep up, old man!

1624
01:49:03,246 --> 01:49:04,747
Nobody would know.

1625
01:49:05,581 --> 01:49:06,624
Nobody.

1626
01:49:08,584 --> 01:49:11,504
"The last I saw him,
an Ultron was sitting on him.

1627
01:49:11,629 --> 01:49:13,506
"Yeah, he'll be missed,
that quick little bastard.

1628
01:49:13,589 --> 01:49:14,590
"I miss him already."

1629
01:49:30,148 --> 01:49:31,315
Hold your fire!

1630
01:49:41,200 --> 01:49:42,243
Romanoff!

1631
01:49:42,744 --> 01:49:43,745
Thanks!

1632
01:49:53,171 --> 01:49:54,756
<i>The anti-gravs are rigged to flip.</i>

1633
01:49:54,881 --> 01:49:57,049
<i>Touch them, they'll go
full reverse thrust.</i>

1634
01:49:57,175 --> 01:49:58,593
<i>The city's not coming down slow.</i>

1635
01:49:58,718 --> 01:49:59,844
Spire is vibranium.

1636
01:49:59,969 --> 01:50:01,095
If I get Thor to hit it...

1637
01:50:01,345 --> 01:50:02,722
<i>It will crack. That's not enough.</i>

1638
01:50:02,847 --> 01:50:04,348
<i>The impact would still be devastating.</i>

1639
01:50:04,515 --> 01:50:05,850
Maybe if we can cap the other end.

1640
01:50:06,058 --> 01:50:07,685
Keep the atomic action doubling back.

1641
01:50:07,852 --> 01:50:09,187
<i>That could vaporize the city.</i>

1642
01:50:10,188 --> 01:50:12,023
<i>And everyone on it.</i>

1643
01:50:17,862 --> 01:50:19,739
The next wave is gonna hit any minute.

1644
01:50:19,864 --> 01:50:21,824
- What do you got, Stark?
- <i>Huh? Nothing great.</i>

1645
01:50:22,658 --> 01:50:24,869
Maybe a way to blow up the city.

1646
01:50:24,994 --> 01:50:26,287
That'll keep it from impacting the surface,

1647
01:50:26,412 --> 01:50:27,455
if you guys can get clear.

1648
01:50:27,705 --> 01:50:29,582
I asked for a solution,
not an escape plan.

1649
01:50:29,832 --> 01:50:32,710
<i>Impact radius is getting
bigger every second.</i>

1650
01:50:32,919 --> 01:50:34,295
<i>We're gonna have to make a choice.</i>

1651
01:50:35,046 --> 01:50:36,547
Cap, these people are going nowhere.

1652
01:50:37,381 --> 01:50:39,842
- If Stark finds a way to blow this rock...
- Not till everyone's safe.

1653
01:50:40,593 --> 01:50:43,596
Everyone up here versus everyone
down there? There's no math there.

1654
01:50:43,846 --> 01:50:45,598
I'm not leaving this rock
with one civilian on it.

1655
01:50:45,848 --> 01:50:47,266
I didn't say we should leave.

1656
01:50:50,102 --> 01:50:51,938
There's worse ways to go.

1657
01:50:57,401 --> 01:50:59,821
Where else am I gonna
get a view like this?

1658
01:51:00,738 --> 01:51:03,324
<i>Glad you like the view, Romanoff.</i>

1659
01:51:03,449 --> 01:51:05,034
<i>It's about to get better.</i>

1660
01:51:29,141 --> 01:51:30,351
<i>Nice, right?</i>

1661
01:51:30,476 --> 01:51:32,937
Pulled her out of mothballs
with a couple of old friends.

1662
01:51:33,062 --> 01:51:34,730
She's dusty, but she'll do.

1663
01:51:35,064 --> 01:51:36,524
Fury, you son of a bitch.

1664
01:51:36,691 --> 01:51:38,943
Ooh! You kiss your mother
with that mouth?

1665
01:51:39,068 --> 01:51:41,279
Altitude is 18,000 and climbing.

1666
01:51:41,445 --> 01:51:42,947
Lifeboats secure to deploy.

1667
01:51:43,072 --> 01:51:45,741
Disengage in three, two...

1668
01:51:46,951 --> 01:51:47,952
Take them out.

1669
01:51:57,628 --> 01:51:59,171
This is S.H.I.E.L.D.?

1670
01:51:59,297 --> 01:52:01,716
This is what S.H.I.E.L.D.
is supposed to be.

1671
01:52:03,384 --> 01:52:04,802
This is not so bad.

1672
01:52:08,097 --> 01:52:09,390
Let's load them up.

1673
01:52:14,812 --> 01:52:16,147
Sir, we have multiple bogies

1674
01:52:16,314 --> 01:52:18,649
converging on our starboard flank.

1675
01:52:18,983 --> 01:52:20,192
Show 'em what we got.

1676
01:52:20,568 --> 01:52:21,569
You're up.

1677
01:52:26,824 --> 01:52:27,825
Yes!

1678
01:52:28,075 --> 01:52:29,827
Now this is gonna be a good story.

1679
01:52:32,496 --> 01:52:34,540
Yup. If you live to tell it.

1680
01:52:34,707 --> 01:52:36,709
You think I can't hold my own?

1681
01:52:36,834 --> 01:52:38,377
We get through this, I'll hold your own.

1682
01:52:38,502 --> 01:52:40,379
You had to make it weird.

1683
01:52:45,217 --> 01:52:48,179
I got about 50 to 100 more
coming in after this group.

1684
01:53:05,112 --> 01:53:06,530
Here we go. Here we go. Let's move.

1685
01:53:06,864 --> 01:53:07,949
Let's go, everyone!

1686
01:53:10,493 --> 01:53:12,495
Number six boat is topped and locked...

1687
01:53:12,620 --> 01:53:14,997
Or stocked... Topped...

1688
01:53:15,539 --> 01:53:16,958
It's full of people.

1689
01:53:18,709 --> 01:53:19,794
Incoming!

1690
01:53:22,838 --> 01:53:23,881
Oh, God!

1691
01:53:34,392 --> 01:53:35,643
<i>You think you're saving anyone?</i>

1692
01:53:37,520 --> 01:53:39,522
I turn that key and drop
this rock a little early

1693
01:53:39,689 --> 01:53:41,774
and it's still billions dead.

1694
01:53:42,233 --> 01:53:43,401
Even you can't stop that.

1695
01:53:43,567 --> 01:53:45,945
I am Thor, son of Odin,

1696
01:53:46,070 --> 01:53:48,406
and as long as there
is life in my breast...

1697
01:53:48,531 --> 01:53:52,076
I am running out of things to say!
Are you ready?

1698
01:53:59,750 --> 01:54:00,876
It's terribly well-balanced.

1699
01:54:01,252 --> 01:54:04,714
Well, if there's too much weight,
you lose power on the swing, so...

1700
01:54:05,673 --> 01:54:08,300
I got it. Create a heat seal.

1701
01:54:08,759 --> 01:54:09,802
I could...

1702
01:54:09,885 --> 01:54:12,263
I could supercharge the spire from below.

1703
01:54:12,430 --> 01:54:13,472
<i>Running numbers.</i>

1704
01:54:23,607 --> 01:54:25,276
<i>A heat seal could work with enough power.</i>

1705
01:54:25,776 --> 01:54:27,778
- Thor, I got a plan.
- <i>We're out of time.</i>

1706
01:54:27,945 --> 01:54:29,155
<i>They're coming for the core.</i>

1707
01:54:29,280 --> 01:54:31,073
Rhodey, get the rest of the people
on board that carrier.

1708
01:54:31,240 --> 01:54:34,452
- On it.
- Avengers, time to work for a living.

1709
01:54:43,544 --> 01:54:44,795
- Are you good?
- Yeah.

1710
01:54:46,297 --> 01:54:47,339
Romanoff.

1711
01:54:47,465 --> 01:54:49,925
You and Banner better not be
playing "hide the zucchini."

1712
01:54:49,967 --> 01:54:51,052
<i>Relax, shellhead.</i>

1713
01:54:51,427 --> 01:54:52,887
Not all of us can fly.

1714
01:54:58,642 --> 01:55:00,311
- What's the drill?
- This is the drill.

1715
01:55:00,478 --> 01:55:02,646
If Ultron gets a hand
on the core, we lose.

1716
01:55:07,234 --> 01:55:09,236
Is that the best you can do?

1717
01:55:19,121 --> 01:55:20,664
You had to ask.

1718
01:55:20,790 --> 01:55:23,125
This is the best I can do.

1719
01:55:23,250 --> 01:55:24,877
This is exactly what I wanted.

1720
01:55:25,252 --> 01:55:26,545
All of you

1721
01:55:26,670 --> 01:55:28,339
against all of me.

1722
01:55:28,589 --> 01:55:30,800
How can you possibly hope to stop me?

1723
01:55:31,675 --> 01:55:33,511
Well, like the old man said...

1724
01:55:34,845 --> 01:55:35,846
Together.

1725
01:57:04,768 --> 01:57:07,146
You know, with the benefit of hindsight...

1726
01:57:16,447 --> 01:57:17,448
They'll try to leave the city.

1727
01:57:17,615 --> 01:57:19,283
We can't let them, not even one. Rhodey.

1728
01:57:19,658 --> 01:57:20,701
I'm on it.

1729
01:57:21,118 --> 01:57:22,494
Oh, no. I didn't say you could leave.

1730
01:57:23,120 --> 01:57:25,206
War Machine coming at you! Right...

1731
01:57:31,587 --> 01:57:32,963
Okay, what?

1732
01:57:33,214 --> 01:57:35,216
We gotta move out.
Even I can tell the air is getting thin.

1733
01:57:35,341 --> 01:57:36,634
You guys get to the boats.

1734
01:57:36,800 --> 01:57:38,594
I'll sweep for stragglers.
Be right behind you.

1735
01:57:38,802 --> 01:57:41,222
- What about the core?
- I'll protect it.

1736
01:57:43,057 --> 01:57:44,183
It's my job.

1737
01:57:45,309 --> 01:57:46,477
Nat.

1738
01:57:46,769 --> 01:57:47,770
This way.

1739
01:57:52,149 --> 01:57:53,317
Get the people on the boats.

1740
01:57:53,484 --> 01:57:54,485
I'm not going to leave you here.

1741
01:57:54,652 --> 01:57:55,694
I can handle this.

1742
01:57:57,988 --> 01:57:59,240
Come back for me when
everyone else is off.

1743
01:57:59,490 --> 01:58:00,950
Not before.

1744
01:58:01,617 --> 01:58:02,701
You understand?

1745
01:58:03,744 --> 01:58:05,454
You know, I'm 12 minutes older than you.

1746
01:58:05,829 --> 01:58:06,914
Go.

1747
01:58:08,499 --> 01:58:10,000
<i>Boss, power levels are way below...</i>

1748
01:58:10,125 --> 01:58:12,294
Reroute everything.
We get one shot at this.

1749
01:58:17,258 --> 01:58:18,509
I know what I need to do.

1750
01:58:18,842 --> 01:58:19,885
The dining room.

1751
01:58:20,177 --> 01:58:21,345
If I knock out that east wall,

1752
01:58:22,096 --> 01:58:23,639
it'd make a nice workspace
for Laura, huh?

1753
01:58:25,182 --> 01:58:26,350
Put up some baffling.

1754
01:58:26,475 --> 01:58:28,644
She can't hear the kids running around.
What do you think?

1755
01:58:28,811 --> 01:58:29,895
You guys always eat
in the kitchen anyway.

1756
01:58:30,020 --> 01:58:31,563
No one eats in a dining room.

1757
01:58:37,236 --> 01:58:38,279
We don't have a lot of time.

1758
01:58:38,946 --> 01:58:40,906
So get your ass on a boat.

1759
01:58:53,877 --> 01:58:55,004
Hey, big guy.

1760
01:58:56,797 --> 01:58:58,549
Sun's getting real low.

1761
01:58:59,091 --> 01:59:01,719
You're safe now.
You're gonna be okay. Buckle up.

1762
01:59:04,263 --> 01:59:05,848
Secure your gear, find a seat.

1763
01:59:05,973 --> 01:59:07,224
Costel!

1764
01:59:08,309 --> 01:59:09,435
We were in the market.

1765
01:59:09,560 --> 01:59:10,602
Costel!

1766
01:59:25,326 --> 01:59:27,369
Thor, I'm gonna need you
back in the church.

1767
01:59:27,494 --> 01:59:28,912
- Is this the last of them?
- Yeah.

1768
01:59:29,371 --> 01:59:31,582
- Everyone else is on the carrier.
- <i>You know, this works,</i>

1769
01:59:32,249 --> 01:59:33,625
we maybe don't walk away.

1770
01:59:34,376 --> 01:59:35,377
Maybe not.

1771
01:59:54,605 --> 01:59:58,108
<i>I got no strings, so I have fun</i>

1772
01:59:58,609 --> 02:00:01,278
<i>I'm not tied up to anyone</i>

1773
02:00:02,863 --> 02:00:04,198
Come on. Time to go.

1774
02:00:36,647 --> 02:00:38,690
You didn't see that coming?

1775
02:01:34,955 --> 02:01:36,707
Oh, for God's sake.

1776
02:01:53,015 --> 02:01:54,766
- Zrinka!
- Costel! Baby!

1777
02:02:07,237 --> 02:02:08,238
No, no, I'm fine.

1778
02:02:08,405 --> 02:02:09,406
Fine.

1779
02:02:11,241 --> 02:02:13,285
It's been a long day.

1780
02:02:27,841 --> 02:02:29,051
Wanda.

1781
02:02:29,760 --> 02:02:33,013
If you stay here, you'll die.

1782
02:02:34,598 --> 02:02:35,974
I just did.

1783
02:02:36,767 --> 02:02:38,519
Do you know how it felt?

1784
02:02:52,616 --> 02:02:54,952
It felt like that.

1785
02:03:29,945 --> 02:03:31,613
Thor, on my mark.

1786
02:03:46,670 --> 02:03:47,671
Now!

1787
02:04:15,699 --> 02:04:18,118
<i>Hey, big guy. We did it.</i>

1788
02:04:19,161 --> 02:04:20,829
<i>The job is finished.</i>

1789
02:04:21,038 --> 02:04:23,707
<i>Now I need you to turn
this bird around, okay?</i>

1790
02:04:28,045 --> 02:04:29,838
We can't track you in stealth mode.

1791
02:04:31,965 --> 02:04:34,092
<i>So help me out. I need you...</i>

1792
02:05:19,763 --> 02:05:20,764
You're afraid.

1793
02:05:21,765 --> 02:05:22,849
Of you?

1794
02:05:23,517 --> 02:05:24,685
Of death.

1795
02:05:25,394 --> 02:05:27,187
You're the last one.

1796
02:05:27,437 --> 02:05:29,898
You were supposed to be the last.

1797
02:05:30,107 --> 02:05:32,401
Stark asked for a savior

1798
02:05:33,443 --> 02:05:35,112
and settled for a slave.

1799
02:05:35,237 --> 02:05:37,656
I suppose we are both disappointments.

1800
02:05:40,117 --> 02:05:41,368
I suppose we are.

1801
02:05:42,077 --> 02:05:43,245
Humans are odd.

1802
02:05:45,080 --> 02:05:48,709
They think order and chaos
are somehow opposites

1803
02:05:50,460 --> 02:05:51,795
and try to control what won't be.

1804
02:05:53,505 --> 02:05:55,966
But there is grace in their failings.

1805
02:05:56,299 --> 02:05:58,218
I think you missed that.

1806
02:05:58,885 --> 02:05:59,970
They're doomed.

1807
02:06:00,887 --> 02:06:01,930
Yes.

1808
02:06:06,143 --> 02:06:09,062
But a thing isn't beautiful
because it lasts.

1809
02:06:11,148 --> 02:06:13,150
It's a privilege to be among them.

1810
02:06:13,400 --> 02:06:15,902
You're unbearably naive.

1811
02:06:16,194 --> 02:06:17,404
Well...

1812
02:06:19,489 --> 02:06:21,533
I was born yesterday.

1813
02:07:34,147 --> 02:07:36,233
<i>Look! Say hi to Auntie Nat!</i>

1814
02:07:37,609 --> 02:07:38,610
Fat.

1815
02:07:39,736 --> 02:07:40,987
One of our tech boys flagged this.

1816
02:07:42,197 --> 02:07:44,366
Splashed down in the Banda Sea.

1817
02:07:45,492 --> 02:07:46,993
Could be the Quinjet.

1818
02:07:47,369 --> 02:07:49,037
But with Stark's stealth tech,

1819
02:07:49,162 --> 02:07:50,705
we still can't track the damn thing.

1820
02:07:52,290 --> 02:07:53,625
Right.

1821
02:07:54,084 --> 02:07:56,336
Probably jumped out and swam to Fiji.

1822
02:07:57,587 --> 02:07:59,464
He'll send a postcard.

1823
02:07:59,756 --> 02:08:01,466
"Wish you were here."

1824
02:08:03,426 --> 02:08:06,721
You sent me to recruit him way back when.

1825
02:08:08,557 --> 02:08:11,101
Did you know then what was gonna happen?

1826
02:08:13,311 --> 02:08:15,230
You never know.

1827
02:08:15,438 --> 02:08:18,942
You hope for the best,
then make do with what you get.

1828
02:08:19,442 --> 02:08:20,902
I got a great team.

1829
02:08:22,028 --> 02:08:23,989
Nothing lasts forever.

1830
02:08:24,281 --> 02:08:26,324
Trouble, Ms. Romanoff.

1831
02:08:26,575 --> 02:08:29,911
No matter who wins or loses,
trouble still comes around.

1832
02:08:33,790 --> 02:08:35,000
<i>The rules have changed.</i>

1833
02:08:35,208 --> 02:08:36,793
We're dealing with something new.

1834
02:08:36,960 --> 02:08:38,253
Oh, the Vision is artificial intelligence.

1835
02:08:38,378 --> 02:08:40,297
- A machine.
- So, it doesn't count?

1836
02:08:40,463 --> 02:08:42,299
No, it's not like a person
lifting the hammer.

1837
02:08:42,549 --> 02:08:44,217
Right, different rules for us.

1838
02:08:44,426 --> 02:08:45,468
- Nice guy. Artificial.
- Thank you.

1839
02:08:45,677 --> 02:08:48,555
He can wield the hammer,
he can keep the Mind Stone.

1840
02:08:49,472 --> 02:08:51,558
It's safe with the Vision.

1841
02:08:51,808 --> 02:08:54,311
And these days, safe is in short supply.

1842
02:08:56,354 --> 02:08:58,315
But if you put the hammer
in an elevator...

1843
02:08:58,440 --> 02:09:00,233
- It would still go up.
- Elevator's not worthy.

1844
02:09:00,358 --> 02:09:02,152
I'm gonna miss these little talks of ours.

1845
02:09:02,319 --> 02:09:03,820
Not if you don't leave.

1846
02:09:04,070 --> 02:09:05,780
I have no choice.

1847
02:09:06,031 --> 02:09:08,199
The Mind Stone is the fourth
of the Infinity Stones

1848
02:09:08,325 --> 02:09:09,701
to show up in the last few years.

1849
02:09:09,826 --> 02:09:11,411
It's not a coincidence.

1850
02:09:12,245 --> 02:09:13,997
Someone has been playing
an intricate game

1851
02:09:14,164 --> 02:09:15,790
and has made pawns of us.

1852
02:09:15,916 --> 02:09:17,792
And once all these pieces
are in position...

1853
02:09:17,918 --> 02:09:19,336
Triple Yahtzee.

1854
02:09:19,544 --> 02:09:21,004
You think you can find out what's coming?

1855
02:09:21,129 --> 02:09:22,213
I do.

1856
02:09:23,048 --> 02:09:24,507
Besides this one,

1857
02:09:24,633 --> 02:09:27,010
there's nothing that can't be explained.

1858
02:09:34,309 --> 02:09:36,853
That man has no regard
for lawn maintenance.

1859
02:09:39,981 --> 02:09:42,609
I'm gonna miss him, though.
And you're gonna miss me.

1860
02:09:42,734 --> 02:09:44,277
There's gonna be a lot of manful tears.

1861
02:09:46,488 --> 02:09:48,114
I will miss you, Tony.

1862
02:09:48,365 --> 02:09:49,366
Yeah?

1863
02:09:49,532 --> 02:09:51,952
Well, it's time for me to tap out.

1864
02:09:52,202 --> 02:09:54,371
Maybe I should take a page
out of Barton's book.

1865
02:09:54,537 --> 02:09:57,457
Build Pepper a farm,
hope nobody blows it up.

1866
02:09:58,249 --> 02:09:59,417
The simple life.

1867
02:09:59,668 --> 02:10:01,962
- You'll get there one day.
- I don't know.

1868
02:10:02,212 --> 02:10:04,589
Family, stability...

1869
02:10:05,757 --> 02:10:08,885
The guy who wanted all that
went in the ice 75 years ago.

1870
02:10:10,387 --> 02:10:12,222
I think someone else came out.

1871
02:10:16,184 --> 02:10:17,268
You all right?

1872
02:10:19,980 --> 02:10:21,398
I'm home.

1873
02:10:29,322 --> 02:10:32,075
You wanna keep staring at the wall,
or do you wanna go to work?

1874
02:10:32,242 --> 02:10:33,576
I mean, it's a pretty interesting wall.

1875
02:10:33,743 --> 02:10:36,746
I thought you and Tony were still
gazing into each other's eyes.

1876
02:10:36,830 --> 02:10:37,872
How do we look?

1877
02:10:38,123 --> 02:10:40,417
Well, we're not the '27 Yankees.

1878
02:10:40,542 --> 02:10:42,252
We got some hitters.

1879
02:10:42,419 --> 02:10:44,796
They're good. They're not a team.

1880
02:10:44,963 --> 02:10:46,589
Let's beat them into shape.

1881
02:11:05,066 --> 02:11:06,609
Avengers...

1882
02:13:25,456 --> 02:13:26,875
Fine.

1883
02:13:28,334 --> 02:13:30,170
I'll do it myself.

